(Phnom Penh): Well-known Cambodian real estate experts have expressed hope for a return to Chinese investment in Cambodia after the recovery of Kovid 19, in which experts raised expectations that China The first and first country to return to invest in Cambodia.
Sorn Sieb, executive vice president of the Cambodian Association of Appraisers and Realtors (CVEA), said that after Kovid 19 was cured, China would be the first country to invest in Cambodia.
"I am convinced that after Kovid's decline in Cambodia, China will be the number one investor in Cambodia," he said. "In general, apart from China, there are other countries such as Korea, Taiwan, Japan, Malaysia, Singapore and Thailand."
He added that the real estate sector is a sector that Cambodia directly benefits from Chinese investment in Sihanoukville and Phnom Penh. In 2020, Chinese direct investment in ASEAN increased by 51%, and for Cambodia, Chinese investment increased by 70%.
Oknha Cheng Kheng, President of CPL Cambodia, said that the agricultural sector in Cambodia is also attracting Chinese investors through the already signed Free Trade Agreement, which will help boost Chinese investment in Chinese agriculture. Need safe agricultural products.
Mr. Lim Socheat, Chairman of the CVEA Board of Directors, also said that for 2022-2023, if Kovid 19 is controlled, the real estate sector will be active again, and purchasing power will have many positive factors.
However, in 2022, the real estate boom will not be as strong as in 2021, as some countries are not yet open to travel, he said. This proves that it is not very good for buying from outside.
He added that currently there are many investors to invest in Cambodia, but Cambodia is not in the Top4 of Chinese investment, out of these four ranks only in Thailand, Singapore, Vietnam and Malaysia. Only. In terms of real estate in Cambodia, it is better than other countries due to the cheaper price and more favorable terms.
"Based on the above factors, Cambodia is still optimistic that when the situation improves, even if it is a little better, Cambodia can still attract foreign investors to invest in Cambodia, especially investment from China," he said. "
"If you look deep into the real estate sector, Chinese investment is looking at areas that can build its community," said CVEA President Chrek Sonim. In Cambodia, China has begun to build two large communities in Cambodia, Phnom Penh and Sihanoukville, which are driving growth.
"Overall, Chinese investment in Cambodia is the first big brother, a big investor in Cambodia, and covers Sihanoukville and Phnom Penh, which is a huge investment in resources and infrastructure, so the sector "Housing and commercial buildings will grow in the future."
According to figures recorded by the Council for the Development of Cambodia in 2020, Cambodia received a total investment of 8,250 million US dollars, of which Chinese investment accounted for 19.74%, equivalent to more than 1,600 million US dollars. Turkey: First two combat helicopters to be delivered to Philippines in September
Two of the six T129 fighter jets that the Philippines has ordered from Turkey will be delivered to the island nation in September 2021. This was released by the Chinese news agency Xinhua on Tuesday evening, May 25, 2021.
According to Turkish media, after the first two units were delivered to the Philippines in September, the next two will arrive in February 2022, while the last two will arrive in February 2023. The Philippines has ordered a total of six T129 combat helicopters from the Turkish company (TAI) at a cost of nearly $ 270 million.
According to the Philippine Ministry of Defense, all of the helicopters it ordered from Turkey were aimed at increasing counter-terrorism capabilities. The Philippines has claimed that it will have more weapons for air strikes in hand.
Sing Bay Otec continues to develop its plantations by planning to plant 10 million commercial trees on an additional 10,000 hectares in 2021
