According to Lu Chu Chhang, the company's plantations have grown well and are a promising hope for Cambodia's agro-industrial plantations.
The President of Sing Bay Otech presented the Company's efforts to develop plantations to serve the wood processing industry in Cambodia and to discuss with the people and communities living in the area who have vacant land to co-plant. Saplings are partners in creating jobs for people and improving their lives.
He also announced the search for other partners to invest in the plantation, as this plantation provides a lot of benefits to the environment and socio-economy.
He said plantations are an important part of contributing to national economic growth, both in terms of job creation and income generation. Neighboring Cambodia and the region, such as Vietnam, earn billions of dollars a year from plantations.
"The advantage of plantations is that they can be harvested from root to tip, and it also contributes to the green cover and plays a vital role in replacing cut natural wood," he said. "Relieve pressure on the use of natural wood."
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Environment said that the growing plantations in Cambodia will help reduce the import of processed wood raw materials from abroad and create a sustainable source of wood for domestic use as natural resources play a role. Importantly, contribute to the preservation of the planet's ecosystem for the people of the world, and Cambodia has strived to protect the timber to sell carbon credits in the voluntary market.
From 2016 to 2020, Cambodia sold $ 11.6 million in carbon credits to be used for forest conservation and community development in protected areas.
