Kovid 19 woman with labor pains, delivery to other hospitals, no last recipient, safe delivery at Russian hospital, patient thanks Phnom Penh Governor for timely intervention
(Phnom Penh): A woman worker of Kovid 19 factory was resting at Chattaly Sak Center, Serey Mongkul Secondary School, Khsach Kandal District, Kandal Province. She was later taken to the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital and delivered safely, both mother and baby.
The factory later contracted 19 cases of Kovid, and his sister, who was pregnant for almost a month, was among those who had to undergo the same procedure. Prek Anchanh on April 22, 2021, when the test result was negative for Kovid.
Born in Anhcheng Leu village, Puk Russey commune, Khsach Kandal district, the health officer, after 19 negative tests for Kovid disease, sent him to continue to work as a cadet at Serey Mongkul's Cadalisak Center with 11 people.
Until May 23, his sister suddenly had a miscarriage (every normal day) and asked for a doctor who was stationed at Chattalysak Center, Serey Mongkul Secondary School. During the examination, the doctor confirmed that the uterus was not open yet, so he had to wait.
On the morning of May 24, with a severe stomach ache, a team of doctors at the Ley Sak Center sent him to the Victory Referral Hospital in Takhmao City, Kandal Province. About an hour later, when he was taken to Victory Referral Hospital, his brother was not yet rested.
After the victory, the referral hospital sent him by ambulance to the Maternal and Child Health Hospital (Japanese doctor), but the Japanese doctor has not accepted him yet. While waiting for the doctor's decision, his sister suddenly burst into tears on the ambulance.
After receiving this information, Mr. Lim Chea Vutha, Director General of Fresh News, contacted Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh to intervene. After receiving the information, Mr. Khuong Sreng contacted the director of the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital to help receive the woman to give birth.
After the intervention, an ambulance carrying the woman left the Japanese hospital for the Khmer-Soviet Friendship Hospital. Upon arrival, a team of doctors dressed as Kovid sent him to the delivery room immediately. About an hour later, after a thorough rescue, a woman named Prich Phanna rested safely while her baby boy weighed more than three kilograms.
According to Prich Mary, the sister of the woman, after giving birth safely, doctors sent her sister and the newborn baby to a separate room. However, she did not know whether the newborn was positive or negative for Kovid 19 and had to wait for a medical examination.
(Stung Treng): The Stung Treng Provincial Land Management Committee this morning, May 25, 2021, held a meeting on the results of the survey and demarcation of natural lake forage, ready to be registered as state property and ready to register Boeung Kilo location. 8 and Kilo 9 Dam Reservoir located in Kilo 8 Village, Sangkat Samaki, Stung Treng City, as additional state property.
The meeting was held at Stung Treng Provincial Hall under the chairmanship of Mr. Mom Saroeun, Governor of Stung Treng Province and the Chairman of the Provincial Land Management Committee, and was attended by the Deputy Governor, the Deputy Director of the relevant specialized units, the Chief of Samaki Sangkat and officials. Many cadastral specialists.
Mr. Ming Sichai, Director of Stung Treng Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, said that in the past, professional officers of the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral Affairs, in cooperation with the relevant authorities, have surveyed and demarcated five lakes. And continue the application process to the State Land Management Commission for registration.
Mr. Ming Sichai continued that in the demarcation of the natural lake area, the professional officer is also continuing the procedure to measure the area of 3 other lakes in Stung Treng province, including Boeung Ralum Prerech Toch, Boeung Veal. Rumpey Thom and O Khlong dams are continuing the procedure and measurements to be completed and submitted to the State Land Management Commission for registration as state property.
Mr. Mom Saroeun supported the registration of the lake area, which the officials and authorities have already measured and demarcated, and requested the Provincial Department of Land Management, Urban Planning, Construction and Cadastral to cooperate with the Provincial Department of Water Resources and Meteorology, together with the relevant authorities in The base expedites the survey and demarcation of natural lakes in the province to be registered as state property.
Mr. Mom Saroeun stated that the registration of natural lake land as state property is in accordance with the Constitution of the Kingdom of Cambodia in order to preserve what is common property, national property to be stable in the long run to avoid loss by encroachment. Illegal by crooks.
