(Kandal): People in Khsach Kandal district, Kandal province, as well as people in other provinces, are being vaccinated against Kovid 19 by the Royal Government of Cambodia. They expressed their pleasure at the opportunity to be vaccinated to prevent Kovid 19, especially thanks to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, for seeking to vaccinate the Cambodian people.
Chap Yuthon, director of Khsach Kandal OD Referral Hospital, told Fresh News that vaccination against Kovid 19 at Khsach Kandal District Referral Hospital began in March 2021. As of May 24, 2021, 5056 people, 2,183 females, were vaccinated.
The vaccination process at Khsach Kandal District Referral Hospital has been observed to be better organized by implementing health protection measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease, such as heat control, alcohol spraying before vaccination and seating arrangements. Safety gaps and so on. These procedures are organized with the help of local authorities.
Mr. Ly Kunthea, Director of the Commune Support Planning Office, said that in order to support the vaccination process to achieve the Royal Government's plan, the district authorities have taken care and cooperated closely with the medical team.
Mr. Ly Kunthea emphasized that the Governor of Kandal Province, Mr. Kong Sophoan, always pays attention and points out to the district authorities to cooperate and prepare plans to facilitate the vaccination work better and prevent the spread of Kovid disease. 19.
Another important operator that makes vaccination work better is the doctors who inject it. At Khsach Kandal District Referral Hospital, as well as at other vaccination sites, the medical team pays close attention to their work. Vaccine doctors are committed to vaccinating without fear of exhaustion and do not charge for Saturdays, Sundays or holidays.
Dr. Huot Phira, a vaccinator at Khsach Kandal District Referral Hospital, said that his team was satisfied with the vaccination. He pointed out that when people get vaccinated, it helps protect them from the risk of contracting Kovid 19 and also helps prevent it from infecting the community.
Not only that, vaccinating local people also helps protect the medical family. Because if people in the community do not have Kovid 19, then it can not be transmitted to the family of doctors.
Vaccines are the most important medicine to protect the lives of people from the spread of Kovid 19, one of the deadliest diseases in the world today. In order to protect the lives of the people from Kovid 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, sought to vaccinate the people.
People who have been vaccinated in Khsach Kandal district consider getting vaccinated as a way to protect themselves against Kovid 19 infection. They expressed their happiness and deep gratitude to Samdech Techo Hun Sen for finding the vaccine to give them.
