National Accounting Council announces change of name to "Accounting and Auditing Regulator" and reminds of the obligation to submit annual financial statements
(Phnom Penh): The National Accounting Council has issued a new notification on the renaming of the Accounting and Auditing Regulator.
According to the announcement received by Fresh News on May 25, according to the Royal Kram No. NS / RKAM / 0121/003 dated 16 January 2021, which promulgated the Law on Organization and Functioning of the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority The National Accounting Council of the Ministry of Economy and Finance is integrated into the Non-Banking Financial Services Authority under the name "Accounting and Auditing Regulators" headed by Director General.
The Accounting and Auditing Regulator will continue to perform the functions and duties of the National Accounting Council as defined in the Law on Accounting and Auditing and the relevant legal documents in force.
In addition, during the preparation of legal documents for the official operation of the Accounting and Auditing Regulatory Institutions, the National Accounting Council logo and seal will be used in documents and documents in official employment relations up to The regulator has its own logo and seal.
At the same time, the Accounting and Auditing Regulatory Authority also issued a separate notification on the reminder of the implementation of the obligation to submit the financial statements for the year 2020 for independent audit and the submission of the financial statements which have been audited independently. Accounting and Auditing.
According to the announcement, any enterprise in points 1 to 4 below is required to submit an annual financial statement for independent audit.
1: Public enterprise 2: Publicly responsible enterprise 3: Qualified investment project 4: Enterprise that is not in points 1, 2 and 3 above but meets both of the three criteria It is obliged to submit the financial statements to an independent audit.
Enterprises that close the accounting period on 31 December and on any day of the second half of 2020, independent audit of the annual financial statements and submission of financial statements to the accounting and auditing regulators are required. Deadline is July 15, 2021.
Failure to comply with these obligations will result in penalties as defined in Sub-Decree No. 79 dated 1 June 2020 on Transitional Penalties for Violations of the Law on Accounting and Auditing and Other Related Provisions. Effective.
