China and Taiwan have been at loggerheads during the COVID-19 outbreak, with Taipei accusing Beijing of spreading false information and trying to block its access to the World Health Organization. WHO) while Beijing claims that Taipei is using the epidemic as a stepping stone to political interests.
However, after months of safety from the COVID-19 outbreak, Taiwan is facing a serious outbreak of the disease and is facing a shortage of vaccines so far. The vaccine is just over 700,000 doses, with a total population of more than 23 million on the island.
In a statement, China's Taiwan Affairs Office said China was "deeply concerned" about the recent outbreak of COVID-19 in Taiwan. Has repeatedly asked for assistance to the island.
Although Chinese vaccines have been used effectively in both China and many other countries around the world, Taiwan, which has repeatedly asked for vaccine assistance from the United States, has stated that it does not. Trust the Chinese COVID-19 vaccine.
The announcement of vaccine assistance and readiness to send experts to Taiwan comes after China saw a number of key Taiwanese politicians urge the island government to order vaccines from China immediately. To solve urgent problems that lie ahead. Taiwan now has a total of 4,917 cases of COVID-19, with 29 deaths and 1,113 recovering, while the average daily infection rate is 300.
General Knowledge: How old are the first human appliances?
(World): As we all know, humans first appeared in Africa about 3 million years ago. Through the ages, they have developed many tools for everyday use, although they are not very modern, but they are also important for the study of their lives. .
Experts have considered and concluded that most of these tools are used in food preparation, such as cutting or slicing meat, scraping fruit peels or tubers.
