Explosion of interest after Stung Meanchey canal, no garbage
(Phnom Penh): There is a lot of interest from people living in Phnom Penh after the Stung Meanchey canal does not have garbage like last year.
Every year at Stung Meanchey canal, when it rains, garbage is often seen floating in the canal, leading to blockage of the flow of water, and the authorities often intervene to facilitate the flow of water.
After a heavy rain on the night of May 23, 2021, the water of Stung Meanchey canal was full. They also noticed that in the area of Stung Meanchey canal, there is no floating garbage ready to seal and accumulate like every year.
It is not yet clear whether the lack of litter in Stung Meanchey due to the people's awareness of the river on littering or due to the closure of Kovid 19 has led to less business activities and reached Less trash?
However, Mr. Sam Piseth, Director of the Department of Public Works and Transport of Phnom Penh, applauded this view. The director of the department considered that this aspect came from the participation of a large part of the people living along the canal who are aware of the garbage disposal.
Mr. Sam Piseth continues to encourage people in Phnom Penh and along the canals to take care of the garbage to be beautiful in Phnom Penh and for people to live healthy.
Please note that under the initiative of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, the Capital Administration has transformed Stung Meanchey Canal from sewage into a clean, odorless concrete canal and can release water from Khan 3 or all areas, and this project will solve the water problem. Submerged in Khan Meanchey, Khan Sen Sok and Khan Por Sen Chey.
The remodeling of the Stung Meanchey canal has been underway since early 2019 and will be completed by 2020.
