Singlang Institute, Siem Reap: Learning English and Chinese at the Same Time is the Key to the Future of Khmer Children
(Siem Reap): Learning English and Chinese at the same time will provide opportunities for Cambodian children to have a bright future as the use of English is the official language for global communication and Chinese is widely used. Extensive to trade relations with China. This was stated by Mr. Eric Wong on May 24, 2021 during the official dissemination ceremony of the Sing Lang Institute in Wat Bo village, Sala Kamroeuk commune, Siem Reap city.
Eric Wong, Founder and CEO of the Singlang Institute, said Singapore more than 50 years ago had a similar situation to Cambodia, but what Singapore has gained today is the organization and development of knowledge. "Education has changed Singapore," he said.
Say Kimseng, a shareholder and director of the Xinglang Institute, points out that English is now considered a universal language and Chinese is considered a commercial language, so both languages are essential for Cambodians as a nation. Developing in line with the Royal Government's policy to turn Cambodia into a high middle income country by 2030 and a high income country by 2050.
In order to participate in human resource development with the Royal Government, this Institute of Foreign Languages has been preparing four types of Singapore-based curriculum, including:
* 1st: 4 levels of basic English * 2nd: 4 levels of basic Chinese * 3rd: Bilingual for communication * 4: Faculty of Teacher Training
At the press conference, local and foreign teachers of the Singlang Institute presented the teaching methods of the Singapore curriculum to make it easier for children and adults to understand and use English and Chinese at the same time. Only proficient for living in today's and future society.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Justice asked Kang Rithikiri's lawyer to correct his re-release immediately because the ministry has never published a criminal book and a code of criminal procedure for sale!
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kim Santepheap, Secretary of State and Spokesperson of the Ministry of Justice, on May 24, 2021, came out to reject the distortion of a lawyer named Kang Rithikiri who posted a message on social media that the Ministry of Justice sold Criminal books and criminal procedure code for $ 100 each.
Through Fresh News, Mr. Kim Santepheap expressed his regret for the irresponsible publication on behalf of Kang Rithikiri, a legal professional, and asked the lawyer to correct his publication. Back immediately.
A spokesman for the Ministry of Justice confirmed to the public that the Ministry of Justice's Code of Criminal Procedure and Code of Criminal Procedure had been published only once during 2013, using French and national funding, and distributed nationwide by Free to all stakeholders, including law enforcement officials and teachers, with no further distribution of this book.
Instead of distributing the Penal Code and the Code of Criminal Procedure, the Ministry of Justice has published the Penal Code and the Code of Criminal Procedure on its official website, which allows both local and foreign citizens to download the official document. There is no charge.
