Mr. Hun Many will lead a delegation to attend a bilateral meeting between young Cambodian National Assembly members and the Chinese National People's Congress online.
(Phnom Penh): After receiving a high note from National Assembly President Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, Mr. HUN Many, Chairman of the National Assembly's Seventh Committee, will lead a delegation of Cambodian National Assembly members to attend a bilateral meeting with Chinese MPs from all over the country. Through the Zoom meeting system on the afternoon of May 24, 2021. This is according to a series of posts on the Facebook page of the 7th Commission on the preparations for the meeting.
The content of the same post also revealed three main topics that were identified for the meeting, including:
Topic 1: "Promoting Peace, Economic Development, Maintaining Multilateralism and Building Prosperity for Humanity by Continuing to Support and Collaborate on All Aspects in the Stages and Post-Kovid 19 Outbreaks"
Topic 2: "Reducing the socio-economic impact of Kovid 19 and enhancing resilience after the global pandemic of the disease, experiences and concepts."
Topic 3: "Strengthen and expand cooperation between the Chinese-Cambodian parliamentary institutions, especially the relationship between the two young parliamentarians towards strengthening the rule of law."
Please be informed that the bilateral meeting between the young Cambodian-Chinese MPs through this video system is aimed at continuing the spirit of the results of the bilateral meeting between Samdech Ponhea Chakrei Heng Samrin, President of the National Assembly of the Kingdom of Cambodia and Mr. Ly Chansou, President of the National Assembly. Representing the Chinese people all over the country on January 18, 2021.
Through the bilateral meeting between the parliamentary leaders of the two countries, as well as the upcoming bilateral meeting between the young Cambodian-Chinese parliamentarians, it is a confirmation of the continuation of the strong Cambodian-Chinese friendship in the legislative sphere. And the executive branch, especially in relations, cooperation, strategic partnership in all aspects between the two countries.
At the same time, the meeting also showed the efforts and high sense of responsibility of the members of the National Assembly of Cambodia, despite the epidemic situation of Kovid 19, still continue to work hard to decide on the necessary work for the common good. For the nation and the people.
