National Bank of Cambodia Introduces Phase 3 Preferential Measures to Mitigate Citizens Affected by Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The National Bank of Cambodia (NBC) has issued a notification on the introduction of the third phase of preferential measures to support the Royal Government's policy to address the challenges and alleviate the burden of people affected by Kovid-19.
According to the announcement received by Fresh News on May 24, 2021, the National Bank of Cambodia has introduced a series of favorable measures to support the Royal Government's policy to solve the problem. Challenge and alleviate the burden of people affected by Kovid 19 in the context of the Kovid 19 outbreak, especially the February 20 community event.
The National Bank of Cambodia has decided to continue the third phase of preferential measures, such as:
1. Maintain the implementation of the obligation reserve at the same rate of 7% until further notice from the National Bank of Cambodia.
2: Allow banking and financial institutions to continue to refinance loans until December 31, 2021. For customers living in the closed area as determined by the Royal Government or the relevant authorities, banking and financial institutions can refinance more than three times during this grace period.
3. Continue to encourage banking and financial institutions to examine the possibility of favorable, easing or waiving any fees or penalties according to the actual situation of customers.
