General Knowledge: Who was the first to travel around the world?
Ferdinand Marceland was a well-known Portuguese sailor who did many things for the Portuguese king, but later moved to serve the king of Spain due to his dissatisfaction with the king of Portugal. Spanish Empire.
In 1517, Macedon abolished Portuguese citizenship and fled to the Spanish monarchy, which was then reigned by King Charles I. In Spain, Macedonia persuaded King Charles I to fund a mission to find a way to the island of Molucc, famous for its strategy and spice trade.
Although he did not reach his goal, he achieved the most difficult navigational courage of all centuries and showed the world and his critics that he could do it. Travel around the world. His discovery opened a new door for a bigger world. "He was the first person to travel around the world."
