(Phnom Penh): The AIDS Health Care Foundation (AHF) will hold a four-day menstrual hygiene event from May 25 to 28, 2021 under the theme "Necessity is not Luxury ”with the launch of a campaign to distribute 5 million tampons to girls and women in need of health care and school attendance.
The AIDS Health Care Foundation, the world's largest HIV / AIDS organization, invites everyone to participate in this's Women's Sanitation Day, as girls, women, men, transgender people and other populations In the reproductive age, up to 1.8 billion people are menstruating every month without proper care about managing their monthly periods.
Women's Menstrual Hygiene Day was recognized worldwide on May 28 and was first established by advocates in 2014 to highlight the importance of menstrual hygiene education. Power to girls to fully participate in society and live a healthy life set by themselves. AHF teams around the world are excited to bring you to this event.
Dr. Houy Sikheng, Program Manager for Cambodia AHF, said that menstrual hygiene issues plague girls' health due to a lack of education, carelessness and inadequate access to sanitary pads. . Breaking the silence, raising awareness and changing negative social norms are very important nowadays.
Access to sanitary pads should be considered a necessity, not a luxury, as lack of access to adequate health and hygiene leads to stigma, harassment and social exclusion, in particular. For teenage girls and young women. We must break down the ancient barriers that hinder this equal right.
