International Biodiversity Day, May 22, was adopted by the United Nations in 2000 and is organized on a variety of topics to promote and raise public awareness of the value of biodiversity and ecosystems.
Mr. Neth Pheaktra added that on behalf of Cambodia as a member of the United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity and to join the Royal Government in preventing the spread of Kovid 19, the Ministry of Environment will celebrate International Biodiversity Day on May 22, 2021. Through an online discussion forum, seven key topics were discussed, including:
* First: Organizing the International Biodiversity Day on May 22 * Second: Research on Cambodia's wildlife * Third: Work experience related to wetland and freshwater biodiversity conservation * Fourth: Improving livelihoods Local communities in protected areas * Fifth: The role and values of biodiversity and solutions * Sixth: Environmental and biodiversity education and 7: Solid waste management and biodiversity conservation.
At the same time, the Ministry of Environment also organized educational videos, short dissemination, as well as the dissemination of images and banners on social media and in public places and towns in Phnom Penh and the provinces, including: Kandal, Siem Reap, Kampong Thom, Kampot, Preah Vihear. Mondulkiri, Sihanoukville and Banteay Meanchey.
This year 2021 is the eighth year that Cambodia has participated in the celebration of the International Biodiversity Day on May 22 in order to promote and raise public awareness and encourage participation in the protection and conservation of natural resources and biodiversity for Sustainable development.
The organization of this day also shows the will of the Royal Government to implement the Rectangular Strategy Phase 4 and the policy of the Ministry of Environment as well as the National Council for Sustainable Development to contribute to the management and conservation of biodiversity and ecosystems, in particular. Cambodia's efforts to engage with the world to implement the United Nations Convention on Biological Diversity.
