Xi Jinping stressed that the fight against COVID-19 is for the people and also for the people. We need to prioritize the safety, life and health of the people, take extraordinary measures to respond to the supernatural with great responsibility and political courage, to truly respect the values and dignity of all. Each.
Xi Jinping emphasized that the outbreak of COVID-19 once again proved that all human beings have the same destiny, so we must adhere to the idea of a healthy human community, unite and work together to overcome On top of all the difficulties, as well as categorically oppose any attempt to turn it into a political story, label it and slander others.
Political manipulation will not be conducive to his country in the fight against COVID-19 at all, will only undermine international cooperation in the fight against COVID-19 and further harm the people of Countries in the world only.
Xi Jinping presented the state of China's global humanitarian activities, pointing out that in the context of limited productivity and huge domestic demand, China has fulfilled its promise by providing vaccine assistance to a number of developing countries. More than 80 are in urgent need and have exported the vaccine to 43 other countries.
China has provided $ 2 billion in aid to developing countries, provided 19 anti-Kovid aids to more than 150 countries and 13 international organizations, as well as provided more than 280 billion masks, more than 3.4 thousand pieces of protective clothing. Millions and more than 4 billion 19 Kovid virus test kits worldwide China and Africa have established 41 cooperation mechanisms between Chinese and African hospitals.
The World Warehouse and Humanitarian Emergency Management Center, co-founded in China by China and the United Nations, has also made significant progress. China has fully implemented the "G20 Debt Consolidation Initiative for the Poorest Countries" with a total of more than 1.3 billion US dollars, the largest debt consolidation among member states. G20.
Xi Jinping announced that China will continue to support new measures for global solidarity against communicable diseases:
First, in the next three years, China will provide an additional $ 3 billion in international aid to support developing countries in the fight against infectious diseases and economic and social recovery.
* Second, China has already provided 300 million doses of Kovid 19 vaccine worldwide, and China will continue to provide more international vaccines to the extent possible.
Third, China supports Chinese vaccine enterprises to transfer technology to developing countries to cooperate in production.
Fourth, China has announced its support for the intellectual property waiver of 19 Kovid vaccines, and China also supports international organizations such as the World Trade Organization to make relevant decisions as soon as possible.
