BEIJING, May 20 (Xinhua) - The European Parliament voted to approve a proposal on an investment agreement between China and the EU before China could release retaliatory sanctions on the European Union (EU).
This is assumed by outsiders that the European Parliament has "frozen" the investment agreement between China and Europe reached through seven years of negotiations. Such an act by the European Parliament is an act of irrational, irrational behavior.
Why did the Chinese side impose retaliatory sanctions on the European side? The reason is that in March this year, the European side unilaterally imposed sanctions on Chinese personnel and relevant units, using lies related to the Xinjiang Uygur Autonomous Region as an excuse to interfere in China's internal affairs. Violated international law and the Basic Code of International Relations.
The Chinese side's retaliation is a need to protect its own interests and is also a right and necessary reaction to resist European sanctions. Whether it is political competition or economic negotiations, intimidation is a commonly used means. But if you want this method to work, the key is to have a scary bet.
Will blocking the authorization of the China-EU investment agreement come into force will scare the Chinese side? It clearly does not happen. As the Chinese side has repeatedly stated, "The investment agreement between China and the EU is a balanced, mutually beneficial and win-win agreement, not a gift to either party."
Over the past 20 years, European enterprise investment in China has reached 146 billion euros and has been very lucrative. The European Parliament acts as a barrier to European enterprises transferring benefits to others.
In addition, blocking investment agreements between China and Europe will have a negative impact on the global economy, which needs to recover immediately. Under the pretext of protecting personal interests, the Chinese side is committed to promoting Sino-European cooperation and achieving win-win.
Therefore, the European side should clearly see the reality, stop sanctions and opposition, use lies as an excuse and make wise choices that are in the interests of all parties.
