Siem Reap Administration Continues 14-Day Night Curf
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration on May 21, 2021 decided to continue the curfew and night business from 8 pm to 5 am for another 14 days. That is, continue this measure until June 4, 2021.
The Siem Reap provincial administration has stated that the implementation of this measure is to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
As of the night of May 20, there were 84 positive cases of Kovid-19 in Siem Reap province. Of those, 36 have been treated, 2 have died and 46 are being treated at the Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital.
The implementation of the curfew was launched on April 10 and has been postponed since the outbreak.
The measures taken by the provincial administration are to temporarily suspend business activities for food stalls, restaurants, cafes, bars and restaurants in hotels, etc. Receiving customers for food, drink or alcohol between 8pm and 5am is limited, but those businesses can be sold packaged.
The measure also temporarily suspends gatherings or gatherings for food, drink or alcohol between 8pm and 5am, except in the following cases:
