The Cambodian team's search operation for ships and unexploded ordnance in submerged rivers and lakes took place after Cambodia successfully completed historic work by successfully retrieving several Marines and tons of unexploded ordnance that sank during During the Civil War, 27.5 meters deep, after operating for 6 months in Veal village, Meanchey commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province.
The second groundbreaking ceremony was held in the presence of General Neang Phat, Permanent Secretary of State of the Ministry of National Defense and Chair of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group to study and resolve the case of unexploded ordnance in the sunken ship. In the river on March 15, 2021.
"At the second site of Boeung Krom, the specialized force is currently attacking the ship's position by taking unexploded ordnance gradually, and the situation at Boeung Krom is different from the site," he said. "First, in Meanchey commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province, because in Boeung Krom, many bullets are large bullets and other dangerous bullets are mixed."
"Most of the more dangerous bullets are mixed, there are no small 12.7 mm bullets or 60 mm or 80 mm bullets, most of them are 105 mm shells," he said. "And rockets that are difficult to retrieve on land."
With the participation of the Permanent Secretaries of State of the Ministry of Interior and the Ministry of National Defense, the Chief of General Staff of the National Police, the Director General of the National Center for Peacekeeping Forces, Demining and War Remnants, the Royal Government delegation in charge of the Director General Phnom Penh Port Autonomous Region All of you are a member of the Inter-Ministerial Working Group.
Samdech Krala Hom Sar Kheng emphasized that according to the instructions of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the inter-ministerial working group to study and solve the case of finding unexploded ordnance in a ship that sank in the river must collect unexploded ordnance. And remove all ships from the bottom of the Mekong River to ensure the safety of people, travelers, fishermen and other businesses along the Mekong River.
General Neang Phat reports to Samdech Krala Hom and the meeting on the results of the closure of the first site in Meanchey commune, Srey Santhor district, Kampong Cham province from October 3, 2020 to April 7, 2021. Successfully, with good cooperation and the highest level of security, the team recovered more than 16 tons of unexploded ordnance and some other weapons.
