(Phnom Penh): The Minister of Commerce of Cambodia, Mr. Pan Sosak, requested the Singaporean side to help promote the export of Cambodian agricultural products to the market in Singapore.
During the meeting, Minister Pan Sosak extended a warm welcome and congratulations to her on her appointment by the Government of Singapore as Ambassador to Cambodia. The Minister and the Ambassador expressed their pleasure and commitment to the close and lasting relationship between the two countries.
The Minister and the Ambassador also discussed and exchanged views on enhancing trade cooperation between the two countries as well as regional trade.
The Minister informed about the potential of Cambodian agricultural products such as mango, banana, longan, Pailin, pepper, Kampot, durian, coconut, dragon fruit and rice. The Minister requested the Singaporean side to coordinate with Singaporean companies in importing agricultural products from Cambodia, as well as to do business matching between Cambodia and Singapore to promote trade in ASEAN.
The Minister praised Singapore's street food sales and asked the Singaporean side to set a good example in organizing such sales as a development initiative for micro and small and medium enterprises, as well as a source of income for Singapore. People.
On that occasion, the Minister and the Ambassador also exchanged views on progress related to bilateral and regional free trade. In particular, the Ambassador also expressed and supported Cambodia in assuming the ASEAN Chairmanship in 2022 and hosting the ASEAN Summit and related meetings. He also informed that Singapore will continue to cooperate with Cambodia as a close friend on all the work raised.
The Minister and the Ambassador reaffirmed their commitment to further strengthen close ties and cooperation in all fields, especially in promoting trade between the two countries.
Singapore is a major regional trading partner for Cambodia. In 2020, despite the context of the crisis caused by Kovid 19, trade between Cambodia and Singapore reached more than 308 million US dollars. Cambodia exported more than $ 87 million to Singapore and imported more than $ 221 million from Singapore.
