(Phnom Penh): The Committee for Research and Investigation of Kovid 19 has allowed the pharmacy "Tapang Thmey Market" to sell medicine normally after checking that the pharmacy has complied with the rules of the Ministry of Health, there is no risk of Kovid 19 infection. From patients who went to buy the mask.
On May 17, 2021, a foreigner who was diagnosed with Kovid 19 went to buy a mask at Tapang Thmey Market. Kovid 19 research team also visited the site to check the situation and assess the possibility of infection or non-infection in the pharmacy.
The research team also checked the status of sales and purchase activities through security camera video. The situation at the store was arranged by the owner of the pharmacy, the customer was tied up, the glass was put in place, the temperature was measured and the alcohol was sprayed.
In addition, the security camera video also showed that when the foreigner who found the positive 19 Kovid went to buy the mask, he was wearing the right mask and kept the distance.
According to Heng Ratha, the owner of the pharmacy, given the state of the market and the security camera footage, the 19-unit Kovid Research Team assessed that his pharmacy was not at risk of infection.
For these reasons, the Kovid Research team also allowed the "Tapang Thmey Market" pharmacy to operate normally and did not require any drug specimens or catalysts. This is the confirmation of Mr. Heng Ratha.
It should be noted that the pharmacy "Phsar Tapang Thmey" used to be required by the authorities to perform a four-day sedation in April, after being involved with 19 positive cases of Kovid. Fourteen days after Chattalysak and no pharmacist became infected, the pharmacy was allowed to reopen.
