The Royal Decree granting political rehabilitation to Mr. Pol Horm and Mr. Phan Chansak follows the obeisance of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, after they submitted a letter to the Ministry of Interior on the 18th. May 2021 to apply for political rehabilitation.
Pol Horm and Phan Chansak were among a total of 118 former CNRP leaders who were banned from politics for five years by a court dissolving the CNRP in connection with the conspiracy. With foreigners to overthrow the legitimate government.
Prior to the re-submission of the letter, it was suggested that Pol Horm was likely to join Ou Chanrath's Cambodian Reform Party. However, Pol Horm could not be reached for comment as his phone was unanswered and had been dialed several times.
Ou Chanrath, a founder of the Cambodian Reform Party, was well aware of Pol Horm's request for political rehabilitation and did not deny the news. But he left it to Pol Horm to announce the matter to the public himself.
In the middle of last month, Yem Ponharith, a former CNRP lawmaker, and Muth Chantha, Kem Sokha's chief of staff, along with five other former party leaders, also received political rehabilitation after submitting a petition. To the Ministry of Interior. Most of those who have been politically trained are close to Kem Sokha, the former president of the Cambodia National Rescue Party.
