Answering a question from the program coordinator about the impact of the 20% tariff exemption, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that without the Kovid 19 epidemic, the removal of the tariff would have had little effect on the Cambodian economy. However, after the 19-crisis Kovid crisis, the 20 percent tariff waiver that the EU withdrew has no effect on the Cambodian economy.
In this international conference, which was attended by leaders and relevant organizations in Asia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen considered the EU decision to be unfair and does not reflect the reality in Cambodia.
Samdech Techo emphasized, "I do not object and do not demand the return of the 20 percent favor. "Cambodia is ready for the non-return of EU favor by not negotiating, not protesting or opposing the implementation of their decisions."
Taking this opportunity, Samdech Techo Hun Sen stated that Cambodia will continue to maintain its political system, a liberal, multi-party democracy, and the upcoming elections in 2022 and 2023 will be attended by many political parties.
