(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, sees that countries in Asia have an important role to play in reshaping the world and the global economy after the Kovid 19 crisis.
The Prime Minister made the remarks at the 26th International Conference on "The Future of Asia" hosted by Japan's Nikkei via video. The conference was held under the theme "Preparing for a New Era after the Kovid Crisis: Asia's Role in Restoring the World."
In his keynote address, Samdech Techo Hun Sen noted some of the crises and challenges facing countries in Asia and the world caused by the 19 19 outbreak of Kovid and other issues.
Samdech Techo highlighted that 2020 is the most difficult year in the modern history of the world due to the outbreak of Kovid-19, which has been causing a serious public health crisis and leading to the disruption of global socio-economic development. Every country and region in the world is suffering in all areas, and more than a hundred million people have been infected and millions have lost their lives.
The Prime Minister said that although the global economy in 2021 is expected to recover, the world still faces high uncertainty due to the risks of the new wave of Kovid-19 and the new transformation. Of the coronavirus, which is more virulent and acute, which may continue to disrupt global economic life.
In his keynote address, Hun Sen also highlighted the obstacles to global economic recovery due to unequal access to vaccines between developed and low-income countries.
"Access to vaccines that can ensure community immunity (Herd Immunity) will take longer, while the gap in access to vaccines between developing and developed countries will widen inequalities," he said. "Economic recovery is due to the fact that only a few countries can recover well, while many others will continue to face both health and economic consequences."
To solve this problem, Samdech Techo Hun Sen saw that countries in Asia have an important role to play.
"Asia is truly a region that has played an important role in paving the way for the post-Kovid crisis with sustainable and sustainable socio-economic development," he said. "Obviously, the Kovid-19 crisis has reaffirmed that Asia is still a region that has the potential and potential to accelerate the recovery of global development."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also drew a number of arguments to show that Asia has a key role to play in rescuing the world after the Kovid 19 crisis.
In addition, before the Kovid-19 crisis, the high growth and rapid development of Asian countries in the last two decades has turned Asia into a major driving force for socio-economic progress, reduction. Poverty and rising incomes of the population.
In this speech, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also gave four points of view in reorganizing the world after the Kovid 19 crisis. The four concepts include:
