(Pursat): Mr. Yom Sophay is one of about 628 veterans who received land and house in Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia and Samdech Honorary Dr. Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Red Cross.
The veteran who fought for the nation against the Khmer Rouge regime in 1978 expressed his excitement to the point of tears when he received the condolences from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit. He said he had never imagined receiving such kindness.
Yom Sophay, 67, was a former Lon Nol military veteran. When the genocidal regime saw the massacre of Cambodians and his relatives by the Khmer Rouge regime, Yom Sophay decided to flee from Koh Thom district, Kandal province, to Pursat province and join the national liberation movement. Genocide of Pol Pot in 1978.
After the country was completely at peace in 1998, he moved to live a simple life. More than 20 years after Cambodia ended the flames of war and prospered, however, the living conditions of Yom Sophay were no different from those of other veterans, not so much.
However, Mr. Yom Sophay, like other veterans, was not left behind and received high attention from Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen.
Mr. YOM Sophay is also a veteran who was selected by the Cambodian Veterans Association to receive land and houses donated by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit in Rany Senchey village, Damnak Troyeung, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province. And stay.
The veteran said that he never imagined or expected to receive such land and house offers from Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit. Mr. Sophay broke down in tears when he talked about receiving gifts such as the merits of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit.
The house and land provided by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are valuable assets for the life of this veteran. Mr. Sophay said that he forbade the sale of his children, even if it was not from him, because this is the most valuable asset for life, an asset from his struggle for the national cause.
It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen decided to cut more than 900 hectares of land in Rany Sen Chey village, Damnak Troyeung, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province to distribute to about 628 families of veterans for living and cultivating crops. At the same time, in the first step, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen decided to provide about $ 500,000, equivalent to 150 houses for the construction of houses for veterans in Pursat province.
About 60 houses have already been built, and authorities have been helping to prepare roads, dig water wells and plant fruit trees such as mangoes, coconuts. Currently, some veterans have come to live on this land and house with the expectation of building a better life.
