The order came after the Minister of Justice received reports that some judges and prosecutors had stopped for more than two to three months without permission. Mr. Keut Rith claimed that the illegal termination, according to Article 52 of the Law on the Statute of Judges and Prosecutors, they had to remove their names from the framework.
Mr. Keut Rith ordered this on the occasion of presiding over the appointment and inauguration of the President of the Phnom Penh Court of Appeal, the President of Kampong Speu Provincial Court, the President of Prey Veng Provincial Court, the President of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Court and the Prosecutor of Prey Veng Provincial Court. .
According to Mr. Keut Rith, the absence of court officials in this way makes many cases congested and hinders the search for justice for the people. He stated that the Royal Government has encouraged the judiciary through the arrangement of appropriate salaries, and for those who have to pay their salaries without going to work without conscience should also be ashamed of themselves.
Mr. Keut Rith also read the Law on the Statute of Judges and Prosecutors in Article 52, which states that if the dismissal or illegal absence of 15 days or more must be disciplined to suspend the salary or leave unpaid. From the day of resignation or the day of absence without permission. If the dismissal or absenteeism is unreasonable for more than 30 days and the judge still does not return to work after two restrictions, the name shall be removed from the framework.
On that occasion, the Minister of Justice also instructed the judges, prosecutors, as well as all court officials to adhere to the five approaches of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, including mirroring, bathing, scrubbing, treatment and surgery, and to adhere to Its determination to properly implement the law for the people.
Mr. Keut Rith further instructed that all officials must participate in promoting the honor, dignity and prestige of the Judiciary by adhering to the discipline, professional ethics of judges, both in their work and in daily life, and participate willingly. Highly responsible for the implementation of the campaign to resolve the congestion of cases in the capital-provincial courts to be accurate, fast and non-corrupt.
Please be informed that Mr. Keut Rith took office as the new Minister of Justice on April 1, 2020. On the day he took office, he announced his commitment to legal and judicial reform in Cambodia in line with the Royal Government's policy to strengthen confidence in the judiciary in Cambodia.
Announcing the appointment of the new Director of Kampot Provincial Department of Women's Affairs, Ms. Huot Ry, to replace Ms. Soeun Sary, who is retiring
(Kampot): Mr. Cheav Tay, Governor of Kampot Province, on May 19, 2021, on behalf of the Minister of Women's Affairs, presided over the inauguration of the new Director of the Department of Women's Affairs of Kampot Province, Ms. Huot Ry, replacing Ms. Soeun Sary. Must retire.
The ceremony was held at Kampot Provincial Hall with the participation of the Deputy Governor, the Prosecutor, the President of the Provincial Court, the Commissioner, the Commander of all kinds of forces, the Director of the Provincial Department, the District Governor and many stakeholders.
Pursuant to Prakas No. 333 KKN / PRK dated 28 April 2021 of the Ministry of Women's Affairs, Ms. Huot Ry was appointed Director of the Department of Women's Affairs of Kampot Province.
On this occasion, Mr. Chiao Tai, Provincial Governor, gave the following 6 important recommendations to Ms. Huot Ry, the new Director of the Department of Women's Affairs:
* First: To continue to implement the remaining work from Ms. Soeun Sary to complete as planned.
* Second: Continue to pay attention to the effective implementation and high sense of responsibility in accordance with their respective roles and responsibilities, as well as strengthen the implementation of laws, regulations and guidelines of the Royal Government, Ministry of Women's Affairs and Provincial Administration. .
* Third: Strengthen solidarity and internal unity with the leaders and civil servants at all levels in the department to be better, that is, to eliminate inactivity and increase the spirit of respect for professional ethics.
* Fourth: To cooperate with departments, units around provinces, municipalities, districts, communes, sangkats to make our work effective, transparent and accountable in order to serve the interests of the Royal Government, ministries and provincial administrations.
* Fifth: When faced with difficulties, report to the leaders of the Ministry and the provincial administration to help solve without leaving those jobs.
* Sixth: Pay attention, encourage, educate, guide, create conditions and provide job opportunities for young officers who are human resources for the next shift in the future.
