BEIJING: An average of 10 million new marriages are registered in China each year, according to data from the Chinese Ministry of Civil Affairs on Wednesday. This was released by the Xinhua News Agency on Wednesday, May 19, 2021.
The Chinese Ministry of Civil Affairs added that each year about 4 million marriage certificates are issued to couples who have not registered their marriage or have lost their marriage certificate. According to the same data, China also sees an average of nearly 4 million divorces per year.
In terms of divorce figures in the first quarter, the number of divorces recorded dropped by more than 70 percent compared to the last quarter of 2020, with 296,000 divorces in the first quarter of this year. In the last quarter of 2020, there were 1.06 million divorces, and compared to the first quarter of 2020, the divorce rate decreased by nearly 52 percent.
