Cambodian, Czech diplomats send congratulatory message on 65th anniversary of diplomatic ties
The Kingdom of Cambodia established diplomatic relations with the former Socialist Republic of Czechoslovakia on 18 May 1956. In 1975, diplomatic relations between the two countries were severed during the Khmer Rouge regime. On September 7, 1996, diplomatic relations between the Kingdom of Cambodia and the Czech Republic were re-established after Czechoslovakia was divided into two countries.
