Another 500,000 doses of Sinovak vaccine will arrive in Cambodia this morning
(Phnom Penh): The additional 500,000 doses of Kovid 19 vaccine from Chinese Sinovak, which the Royal Government of Cambodia has ordered, will arrive in Cambodia on Sunday morning, May 16, 2021.
The 500,000 doses of Sinovak vaccine delivered to Cambodia this morning is the fourth vaccine ordered by the Royal Government of Cambodia, while the first dose of 1.5 million doses was delivered to Cambodia on March 26. The second leg delivered 500,000 doses to Cambodia on April 17 and the third leg delivered 500,000 doses to Cambodia on May 11.
The Kovid 19 vaccine is seen as an additional important tool in the fight against Kovid 19 and helps protect human health from Kovid 19 attacks. The Royal Government of Cambodia has launched a strategy to vaccinate its people as soon as possible. At the same time, the Royal Government seeks vaccines and brings in a series of vaccines for its citizens.
It should be noted that Cambodia has already received more than 4.5 million doses of vaccines, including: 1.7 million doses of Sinofam, a grant from the Chinese government, 2.5 million doses of Sinovak purchased from China, and 324,000 doses of AstraZenica vaccine. Cowboys through the World Health Organization.
Cambodia started vaccinating people on February 10, and so far more than 2 million people have been vaccinated. The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has stated that he will seek more than 20 million doses of vaccines for more than 10 million people to build immunity.
For 2021, there will be a series of vaccines coming to Cambodia for people to inject. As planned, on May 23, Cambodia will receive 1 million doses of vaccine, June 3 million doses, July 2 million doses, August 1 million doses.
Cambodia has become the second largest country in ASEAN after Singapore, a country that has vaccinated its people faster and more. The presence of the vaccine will enable Cambodia to achieve its immunization plan, which aims to reach an estimated 13 million people by the first half of 2022, with the expectation of a successful Kovid 19 mission. To improve the economic situation.
