Beware of losing to crooks! Woman steals 8 cigarettes from a seller in Kraing Thnong
(Phnom Penh): It can be said that sharing an experience for grocery sellers to be very careful of crooks when they come to play tricks in the store. On Friday, May 14, 2021, a grocery seller named "Pich Chenda", a wholesaler and retailer of drinks and groceries in Sangkat Kraing Thnong, Khan Sen Sok, was cheated by a crook. Goods and stole 8 cigarettes and disappeared.
The owner of the grocery store described that at around 9:40 this morning, a woman over 40 years old, riding a motorcycle with no license plate and license plate, came to shop at her stall. . The woman pretended to order a variety of items at no cost, including buying eight packs of cigarettes, each of which sold for 5,000 riel.
According to the shop owner, the scam seems to have been premeditated because the wording, order and time gap seem to be very similar.
Through this experience, the victim shop owner called on other shop owners to be very careful to avoid cheating like in the above case.
(Phnom Penh): Mrs. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission on Vaccination, said that the vaccination against Kovid 19 may be launched throughout Phnom Penh this May.
Ms. O Vandin confirmed this in an interview with the media when the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, handed over 1 million and 2 million vaccinated people on the afternoon of May 14, 2021.
In the interview, she pointed out that the 14-day vaccination in the red zone in the six districts by the army is almost complete, and the second dose will start on May 15.
She also stated that next week, after Cambodia receives an additional 1.5 million vaccines, the Ministry of Health's medical team will start vaccinating in two other districts, Sen Sok and Boeung Keng Kang. After these districts will proceed to the next district.
"We hope that this month we will start all the districts in Phnom Penh," she said.
In addition to the start of vaccinations in all districts throughout Phnom Penh, Ms. O Vandin also confirmed that the vaccines that arrive in the next month, the Committee for Vaccination will continue in Kandal, as well as Sihanoukville and the province. Follow up as directed by Samdech Techo.
The Royal Government of Cambodia started vaccinating people on February 10, and by May 14, Cambodia has vaccinated more than 2 million people, equivalent to about 20 percent of the more than 10 people who have been vaccinated. Millions.
Ms. Ovandin said vaccination was one of the government's plans and strategies to overcome the spread of Kovid 19. In particular, help the Cambodian economy continue to function.
In this spirit, the Royal Government, through the Council for the Economy of Cambodia, chaired by Deputy Prime Minister Aun Porn Moniroth, as well as the Vaccination Commission, has put in place a balanced strategic plan on how to vaccinate key areas of the economy. In Cambodia.
(Phnom Penh): Ms. O Vandin, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Commission for the Kovid 19 Vaccination, called on the people not to rejoice with the declining rate of Kovid 19 infection and to remain vigilant. Do not let the virus spread again. What makes her even more cautious is the new Kovid 19 virus.
The 19 cases of Kovid 19 in the community event on February 20 over the past three months have resulted in a steady increase in the number of cases so far, bringing the total number of Kovid 19 cases in Cambodia to 21. , 499 people and up to 147 deaths.
However, under fierce fighting efforts under the leadership and command of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Commander-in-Chief of the Shadowless Battle of the Enemies, 19 Kovid cases in 20 community events were seen to decline over a period of time. The last 3 days in a row.
