Vendors of vegetables, fish and meat at Serey Stong Market protested to keep sales at Serey Stong Market after the authorities organized order
(Kampong Thom): Vendors of vegetables, fish and meat at Serey Stong market in Kampong Thom province protested to keep sales at Serey Stong market after the authorities organized order.
Vendors said they supported the authorities' order not to sell on the streets by selling according to the diagrams provided by the authorities. In particular, you just ask the authorities to open the way for cars that carry vegetables, fish, meat as usual.
Normally, the order of Serey Stong market is along the road where the traders take the public road to sell, which causes traffic congestion and loss of order, loss of beauty and non-compliance with the instructions of the Ministry of Health. Security gaps in the context of Kovid 19.
He added that this arrangement has lost some of the benefits of those who used to take street food and front of the house to rent to other vendors, which makes them spend a lot of money.
He said that the district authorities have cooperated with Stong Aphivath Market to find a place for them to sell vegetables, fish and meat on the road and feed in front of their houses to sell properly, have a clean yard and no Paid and no coercion.
If anyone wants to come and sell at Stong Aphivath Market, they can or will not come to sell at will, but must respect the arrangements of the authorities. At the same time, people who used to shop at Serey Stong Market changed to shop at Stong Aphivath Market, saying that they came to sell here, there is a clean place and no one is forcing them, and this place has no payment No, so please come and sell here to have a decent place to shop.
Ministry of Environment asks all provincial governors to stop certifying land tenure in natural resource protection areas
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Say Sam Al, Minister of the Ministry of Environment, requested all Capital-Provincial Governors to immediately stop and annul any signing or confirmation of land tenure in natural resource protection areas, including the Biodiversity Conservation Corridor. All.
According to the letter of the Ministry of Environment dated May 10, 2021, received by Fresh News on May 14, 2021, stated that the Ministry has recently found that some commune administrations are still down. Signature certifying the recognition of the title deed, the application for possession and use of the land, the title deed for the sale of state land for ownership within the protected area and the biodiversity conservation corridor, both illegally.
The letter said that in order to prevent and deny the influence of those documents, all capital and provincial governors must take action by rejecting and annuling all documents or documents related to the occupation and transfer of rights. On land located in a protected area.
