Mr. Sik Bunhok, Chairman of the NEC, assigned several working groups of the General Secretariat of the NEC, led by Mr. Dim Sovannarom, Member and Spokesperson of the NEC, to participate in this Seoul International Forum. Lessons and experiences for preparing for the upcoming elections in Cambodia in the context of Kovid 19.
This international forum focuses on two topics:
First: The Crisis of Democracy and Building Confidence in Elections
Second: The role and responsibilities of social media in elections
Regarding the crisis of democracy and confidence-building in elections, the Seoul International Forum said the public health crisis has prompted authorities to restrict freedoms and fundamental rights to ensure the safety of voters.
In this forum, other speakers also shared the key points in some of the countries that held elections in the context of Kuwait 19 and still maintain the same voter turnout or higher in the absence of the Kuwait 19 outbreak as follows:
Revise regulations and procedures in accordance with measures to prevent Kovid. 19-Train election officials to better understand the situation and prevent Kovid.
* After the election:
This participation is really important as the NEC is preparing to hold elections in the context of Kovid 19, the first election to elect the Bokor City Council, which will take place on July 25, 2021.
The Seoul International Forum for Elections 2021 in the context of Kovid 19 provides some new inputs for the NEC to prepare for free, fair and secure elections. In addition, the rich use of social media in Cambodia, the experience of the Seoul International Forum is a new entry point for the NEC of the Kingdom of Cambodia.
All this is also in preparation for the 2022 Commune / Sangkat Council Election and the upcoming 2023 National Assembly Election, if Kovid 19 continues to shake Cambodia and the world.
