Commentary: The United States and the United Kingdom can not represent the United Nations and even more can not represent the international community.
People who know the history of Xinjiang are well aware that the real issue of Xinjiang issues is counter-terrorism and the elimination of extremism, not the human rights issues that a small number of Western countries often inflate. . If we want to talk about human rights, we can make the following comparison.
Take the work of preventing and controlling the spread of Kovid 19 as an example. A spokesman for the Chinese Permanent Mission to the United Nations has released figures showing that Xinjiang, with a population of more than 25 million, has found a total of 980 cases of Kovid 19 infection, 977 cases of cure and death. 3 people. In the United States, the death toll was nearly 600,000, with Britain at more than 120,000 and Germany at more than 80,000.
A small number of Western countries cannot guarantee the right to life of their own people. What qualifies to criticize the human rights situation in Xinjiang? A small number of Western countries can not represent the United Nations and even more can not represent the international community.
At the 46th General Assembly of the UN Human Rights Council, more than 80 countries, including Islamic countries such as Saudi Arabia and the United Arab Emirates, voiced various forms of support for China's position. In issues related to Xinjiang.
