Cambodia and ASEAN Chairmanship 2022: Opportunities and Preparations for the ASEAN Political-Security Community Building Process
Since Cambodia joined ASEAN in 1999, ASEAN has always been an important part of Cambodia's foreign policy. Over the past 20 years, Cambodia has seized many opportunities from its membership in ASEAN, and Cambodia has also made significant contributions to building the ASEAN Community in general and the ASEAN Political-Security Community in particular. .
Since Cambodia became a member of ASEAN in 1999, Cambodia has chaired ASEAN twice, the first time in 2002 and the second time in 2012, and in 2022 Cambodia will To chair ASEAN again. As chair of ASEAN in 2022, what are the opportunities for Cambodia in the process of building the ASEAN Political-Security Community? What kind of preparations should Cambodia make to seize those opportunities?
Cambodia, formerly known as the Killing Fields, as an insecure area, as a dreaded minefield, is now a "Peace Island" and a popular tourist destination in Southeast Asia. Millions a year.
The above are some of the opportunities that Cambodia can get as the chair of ASEAN in 2022. But the question is, how should Cambodia prepare to seize those opportunities?
As chair of ASEAN, Cambodia will have both opportunities and challenges. In this sense, Cambodia must be prepared both internally and externally enough to seize opportunities and meet challenges. Here are some considerations about Cambodia's readiness as chair of ASEAN.
In addition, Cambodia needs to set an agenda that can provide tangible benefits for ASEAN citizens, so that ASEAN citizens can be proud and hopeful for the future and confident for the well-being of the next generation, and try to strike a balance between The three pillars of ASEAN are the political-security community, the economic community and the socio-cultural community.
By: Dr. Kin Phea, President of the Institute of International Relations of Cambodia, Royal Academy of Cambodia
