During the meeting, Mr. Pan Sosak expressed his deepest condolences to the Government and the people of India on the outbreak of the Kovid 19 epidemic and the deaths of many Indians due to this global epidemic.
Regarding trade between Cambodia and India, Minister Pan Sosak and Indian Ambassador discussed the progress of the establishment of the Cambodia-India Bilateral Trade Agreement, which is currently being worked out by the two countries' working groups. Terms of reference for the Trade Negotiation Committee of this Agreement.
The Minister and Ambassador highly appreciated the cooperation in all fields, especially the cooperation to promote the establishment of a joint working group on bilateral trade and investment.
The Minister as well as the Ambassador expressed the same view on the importance of increasing bilateral trade, which is an important pillar in strengthening bilateral relations. The two sides also agreed to continue to strengthen ties to resolve any issues that may arise and to continue to work closely together both regionally and internationally.
According to a report by the Ministry of Commerce, in 2020, the trade volume between Cambodia and India reached more than 190 million US dollars. Of that, Cambodia exported more than 61 million US dollars and imported from India nearly 129 million US dollars.
