Sputnik is nearly 56 cm in diameter and weighs more than 80 kg. It orbits the Earth every hour and 36 minutes at a speed of nearly 30,000 kilometers per hour. Sputnik has an elliptical orbit, with the nearest point being 230 km and the longest distance being nearly 1,000 km. In January 1958, Sputnik returned to Earth's atmosphere as planned and the fire disappeared in the atmosphere.
Commentary: Census data across China breaks 'words about population crisis'
BEIJING (Reuters) - The world's largest probe project announced the results on May 11. The same day, the Chinese government officially released key data from the seventh national census, showing that by 2020, China's total population will reach 1.41 billion. That's about 18 percent of the world's population and still ranks first in the world.
According to the latest census data, the situation does not seem so pessimistic. Over the past 10 years, China's total population has grown by 7,260,000. People. At present, China has 8.80 million adult workers between the ages of 16 and 59, and the labor force is still very rich. The average age of the Chinese population is 38.8 years, which is about the same as America.
Whether fertility rates are declining or society is aging, in fact, this is a common challenge facing the whole world. In particular, Chinese society is preparing psychologically and politically to meet the relevant challenges. For example, referring to the social problems of the elderly, China is developing an "aging economy" and expanding products and services for the elderly.
