Rafidah is celebrated by Muslims all over the world every year after the end of Ramadan, when all Muslims fast, pray and practice the right religion for a whole month.
According to the proclamation of the Supreme Council of Islam of Cambodia, Thursday, May 13, 2021 is the day of Riyadh for the Muslims of Cambodia in 1442 A.D. If we look at the world, we also see that it is also a Raya day for Muslims around the world.
The day of Riyadh falls on the first day of the tenth month in Islam, after Ramadan, the month when Muslims fast on food, lust, and other evils. The day of Raya Haji is on the 10th day of the month of Tul Hajj or the month of Hajj, the 12th month of Islam for Muslims who are able to go to Hajj in Makkah, Saudi Arabia.
