* Professor: This Raffa Day reflects the following values:
* 2. Raya Day is a day of charity in Islam, which can be called a day of donation, because on that day, all Muslims, young and old, men and women, have to donate about 3 kg of rice. The poor or the equivalent of money to give pleasure to the poor on the day of Raya.
* Raya Day symbolizes unity in Islam because Muslims around the world practice the same Riyadh salutation after the same fasting in Ramadan.
* Raya Day symbolizes equality in Islam It is a day when Muslims express their joy and friendliness to each other, regardless of status, merit, position, wealth or prestige.
* 5. Raya shows that Islam wants its followers to be successful and happy in both the world and the afterlife.
* 6. The day of Raya shows respect for the Muslim leadership, because Muslims in general are always waiting to hear the announcement of the Muslim leadership about the time of the day of Raya by seeing the Qur'an or through recitation. 30th day of Ramadan in case of invisibility of Savannah on the evening of the 29th day of Ramadan.
