(Phnom Penh): General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chairman of the Vaccination Team in the Red Zone, told Fresh News that the first dose in the Red Zone in Phnom Penh has reached about 80 percent. The second dose is scheduled to begin on May 15.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Head of the Royal Government of Cambodia, issued an order to the Vaccination Team of the Ministry of National Defense to launch a vaccination campaign in the red zone in six districts, including: Kampoul, Dangkor, Por Senchey, Meanchey, Toul Kork and Russey Keo yesterday. May 1 ago. The vaccination process in the Red Army, operated by the army, has been noted to be rapid, with around 50,000 people being vaccinated daily.
General Ith Sarath, the operator of the vaccination operation in the red zone, pointed out that some districts, such as Kambol and Dangkor, had already been vaccinated and only a few remained. Separately, in Po Sen Chey and Meanchey districts, some communes, which are the gathering areas of factories and gathering places for workers, are not ready yet.
According to General Ith Sarath, the communes where the factories and workers were gathered were Sangkat Stung Meanchey 1, Sangkat Stung Meanchey II of Khan Meanchey and Sangkat Choam Chao I and Choam Chao II of Por Sen Chey.
In order to vaccinate workers in these four communes in a timely manner, General Ith Sarath decided to mobilize 12 vaccination teams from other areas to be vaccinated in this area. According to General Ith Sarath, there are five large factories in these areas with up to 95,000 workers.
General Ith Sarath confirmed that "we take the force that has been injected from other communes together, we increase to the red area in Sangkat Choam Chao 1 and Sangkat Choam Chao 2, Khan Por Sen Chey and Sangkat Stung Meanchey 1 and Sangkat Stung Meanchey 2, Khan Meanchey." .
General Ith Sarath also pointed out that in order to facilitate the injection process in these areas, the vaccination team has also set up vaccination sites to make people more isolated, not wanting them to travel far, which could lead to the spread of Kovid 19.
The director of the Ministry of National Defense's Red Vaccination Operation, General Ith Sarath, confirmed that the second dose will proceed as planned on May 15. Although the second dose is given, the first dose for those who have not been injected will continue.
"Our team has worked hard to implement consistently and quickly in accordance with the regulations and plans set out by Samdech Techo and the direct guidance of Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh. "So on May 15 or 16, we will be able to give the second dose to the people." This is the additional confirmation of General Ith Sarath.
According to the planned data, a total of 798,461 people will be vaccinated in the red zone in the six districts. But according to Ith Sarath, the actual number has now risen to nearly 100,000.
Vaccination for 12 days in the red zone, more than 500,000 people have already received the first dose.
The Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, has expressed great satisfaction with the military's operation on vaccination in the Red Zone due to its rapid and orderly vaccination. Samdech Techo also announced that he will vaccinate the people in this red area until all.
Getting vaccinated is one of the most important health benefits to fight as well as prevent Kovid 19 infection. Vaccinated residents also expressed satisfaction and joy.
They also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen for allowing them to be vaccinated. They also thanked the Ministry of Defense's vaccination team for paying close attention to the vaccination work. China administers more than 342 million doses of vaccine to its people nationwide
