Nearly 12 Tons of Counterfeit Alcohol or Methanol Destroyed by Ministry of Commerce Officials After Market Crackdown
In fact, on May 11, 2021, an official of the General Department of KP Nearly 12 tons of counterfeit alcohol or methanol was destroyed at a landfill in Phnom Penh's Dangkor district.
The demolition ceremony was organized with the approval of the Phnom Penh Municipal Court and with the participation of Dangkor district administration officials. These methanol substances are the official of the General Department of PPR. Inspected and confiscated from warehouses, means of transportation and pharmacies in Phnom Penh.
Alcohol, or ethanol, is a substance that is used to kill germs, especially at a time when Kovid 19 is on the rise. ) To sell to people to kill germs or as an ingredient for making antiseptic gel.
The chemical methanol is a toxic substance that is often used as a solvent. The use of methanol as an antiseptic is not only ineffective in killing germs, but also causes harm to the user's health, such as skin irritation, eye irritation, headache, dizziness, blurred vision, drowsiness, loss of consciousness, nausea and vomiting. Digestion or can be fatal if mixed with alcohol and consumed in excess.
Once again, the General Department of the DPRK We call on all wholesalers, retailers, pharmacists, supermarket owners and importers of alcohol products to conduct their business responsibly, adhere to ethics and integrity, and consider the welfare of the people above all else. Its profit.
