Letters from readers: Cambodia in the spirit of solidarity against Kovid 19
This article outlines the role, commitment and efforts of the Royal Government of Cambodia in mobilizing resources and investing in national campaigns to save lives and lead the country out of this global crisis.
Despite the devastating and devastating effects of the February 20 events, the Cambodian people have shown resilience and national unity, and the Royal Government remains committed to protecting the country against this rare epidemic. National and sub-national authorities, as well as other state institutions, have been actively working to save lives and reduce the negative impact of the epidemic.
Cambodians also demonstrated their civic duty and culture of sharing by donating more than $ 56.9 million in cash to the Royal Government's Fund for Vaccine Purchase. Their contribution through large donations to the defense of the nation is a sign of encouragement and optimism for the country's future. The Queen Mother and the King donated four times in cash, totaling $ 3,700,000.
