58 houses completed by Samdech Techo and Samdech Kitti for veterans in Pursat province
(Pursat): 58 houses, which are warm shelters for veterans in Pursat province, donated by the Prime Minister of Cambodia Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittiprittbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, have been completed and 68 projects have been completed. Back.
Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit donated about $ 500,000 for the construction of 164 houses on a social land concession in Say village, Prongel commune, Phnom Kravanh district, Pursat province, distributed to disadvantaged Cambodian veterans Shelter.
On May 9, 2021, Senior Minister Kun Kim, Vice President and Secretary General of the Veterans Association, inspected the construction process of houses and infrastructure in the area.
Senior Minister Kun Kim stated that at the request of the Association to solve the hardships of the lives of about 600 families of Cambodian veterans in Pursat province, Samdech Techo has provided social land concessions at the above location and Samdech Kittiprittbandit has been responsible for the construction. Home to them.
The Senior Minister, on behalf of Samdech Techo's staff on the work of Cambodian veterans, said that currently the process of building houses and infrastructure here is being carried out carefully by stakeholders. Get it done as soon as possible and allow the families of Cambodian veterans to stay.
According to Kun Kim, in addition to building houses, the Ministry of Rural Development and Pursat provincial governor Mao Thanin helped build roads, dig wells and pave the land for veterans there.
In addition, the Pursat provincial administration has established an alliance between provincial departments and institutions with the veterans' new villages to support the development and facilitate the lives of veterans. This was confirmed by Senior Minister Kun Kim.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit are leaders who have taken great care of Cambodian veterans who sacrificed their lives for the cause of the motherland during the Cambodian civil war crisis. In return for this merit, Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit have already established tens of thousands of homes for Cambodian veterans across the country.
Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit always urge the relevant authorities to pay attention and support so that the veterans, most of whom are elderly and disabled, can live a decent life in a peaceful society earned by the sacrifice of They.
During the visit to inspect the construction of houses and villages of Cambodian veterans in Pursat province, Senior Minister Kun Kim urged all working groups to pay attention to the construction and organization of villages.
Senior Minister Kun Kim also reminded of the spirit of consideration and remembrance for Cambodian veterans. He said that despite the circumstances, the Cambodian nation was suffering from Kovid 19, but Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit did not forget the Cambodian veterans. Both Samdechs often remind him to pay attention to the living conditions of Cambodian veterans and to manage to solve their shortcomings and difficulties in a timely manner.
