Police arrest 42 vehicles and a tricycle for smuggling workers out of the red zone in Por Sen Chey district, arresting more than 100 people
(Phnom Penh): Police forces launched an operation to seize 42 vehicles and a tricycle in violation of instructions by smuggling workers out of the red area in Por Sen Chey district, Phnom Penh this morning, May 08, 2021.
A report from the Po Sen Chey District Police Inspectorate, obtained by Fresh News, stated that in addition to seizing the means, police also detained a total of 104 people, including 49 workers and 55 truck drivers, including children. Three small ones.
Of the more than 100 people, 49 were workers and 55 were drivers and truck drivers, police said.
Please be informed that the decision of the Phnom Penh Capital Administration during the implementation of this blockade measures, all persons living in the red zone are prohibited from leaving their current residence or lodging, including not being allowed to do so. Sports activities outside their home or residence, except in case of emergency.
Mr. Mean Chanyada, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, who personally carried out this work, confirmed that under the direct command of Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh and Chairman of the Phnom Penh Municipal Unity Command, 55 taxi drivers and 42 vehicles were arrested. A total of 104 people, 49 of them, were detained as they stormed out of the restricted area (red zone) with the intention of traveling to the provinces.
Mr. Mean Chanyada added that all 104 of them were sent for 14 days to be vaccinated at Kok Panchan Secondary School with Kovid-19 sampling.
At the same time, he appealed to other people living in the red zone not to do anything wrong like the 104 people above, do not try to leave the red zone, which is a high risk area of the outbreak. Kovid-19 disease. He asked all people to follow the instructions of the authorities as well as the competent forces to stop the spread of Kovid-19 disease together.
