This statement was made by Mr. Wang Vin Thean during the official inauguration ceremony of fresh mango export from Cambodia directly to China under the presidency of Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on the morning of May 7, 2021. This.
"By opening up the Chinese market for Cambodian mangoes, there will be as much growth as bananas," Wang said.
He added that China has high market demand and advanced agricultural productivity, and China has become the largest export market for Cambodia.
He said that after the successful export of Cambodian bananas to China, banana production in Cambodia has developed significantly and the volume of exports has increased from 10,000 tons in 2018 until 330,000 tons in 2020.
The Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia believes that under the joint efforts of the two countries, more Cambodian agricultural products will be able to be exported to China.
He stressed that agricultural operations between the two countries will be able to reach a new stage, which will contribute to the comprehensive development between the two countries.
At the same time, he also stated that despite the Kovid-19 crisis, under the leadership of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, the agricultural sector in Cambodia has achieved growth in 2020.
Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries Veng Sakhon confirmed that in the first year, Cambodia expects to export about 100,000 tons of fresh mangoes to the Chinese market, earning about $ 100 million.
Mr. Veng Sakhon said that the export of 100,000 tons in the first year is just the beginning, but for the next year, he believes that the volume will increase significantly and about 10 new packaging plants will be ready to be delivered. Also works.
