Saudi Arabia allows only those who have been vaccinated to return to work, whether public or private
Riyadh: Saudi Arabia on Friday announced that only vaccinated staff will be allowed to return to their workplaces. This is according to the release by the AFP news agency on Friday, May 7, 2021.
The Ministry of Human Resources and Social Development said in a statement that vaccination would be a necessary condition for the return of public and private workers to their workplaces, urging them to get vaccinated. Everyone.
So far, Saudi Arabia has administered more than 10 million doses of the vaccine in a country of more than 34 million people, the health ministry said.
Phnom Penh Governor Facilitates Reduction of Room Rent and Provides Additional Food to Factory Workers in Red Area
(Phnom Penh): After receiving information from workers living in a rented house along Veng Sreng in Village 2, Sangkat Steung Meanchey 3, Khan Meanchey, who had a shortage of food and also had problems related to the price of a rented house on the evening of the 7th. In May 2021, Phnom Penh Governor Khuon Sreng led Khan and Sangkat authorities to coordinate with these workers, with the landlord agreeing not to increase the room rate.
According to social media sources, the workers who lived there confirmed that they had rented 470 rooms at the above location, and after the February 20 community event, the landlord reduced the rent by 20. Dollars per room offered to share their hardships while the factory was closed.
But lately, after the government has reopened traffic, landlords' rents have risen, leaving workers living in the red zone unemployed. Disagree with this price increase. The protest, after mediation from the governor of Phnom Penh, the landlord agreed with the authorities to reduce the price of $ 20 back to the original.
At the same time, Mr. Khuong Sreng also supported the 470 workers in each room, each room received a gift from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, 1 bag of rice weighing 25 kg, 1 box of noodles, 10 cans of fish and 1 can of fish sauce. These gifts will be distributed in front of the workers' rented room.
(Siem Reap): The former capital of Angkor Thom has an area of 9 square kilometers, which was built in succession during the reign of many kings and continued until Jayavarman VII.
The former capital is surrounded by four walls, each 3 km long. The four corners also have five main gates facing the four main directions: the east has the Chey Gate and the Ghost Gate, the West has the Gulf Gate, the South has the Om River Gate, and the North has the Earthen Gate. Next to the outer wall is the surrounding water tank.
In the center of the former capital of Angkor Thom is a unique Bayon temple built by Jayavarman VII. The top of Bayon temple has four-faced Brahma sculptures facing the four major directions and has shown a never-ending smile to tourists of all nationalities, as well as elevated the national cultural values to a greater value forever.
