The first day of exporting fresh mangoes to China from 6 containers equal to 80 tons.
Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, who attended the official inauguration of fresh mango exports to China, said that in the first year, Cambodia expects to export about 100,000 fresh mangoes to the Chinese market. Tons through the capacity of five packaging companies approved by the General Department of Customs of China.
Mr. Veng Sakhon said that the export of 100,000 tons in the first year is just the beginning, but for the next year, he believes that the volume will increase significantly and about 10 new packaging plants will be ready to be delivered. Also works.
Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia Wang Winthean considers the official export of fresh mangoes to China to help improve the livelihoods of mango farmers, as well as yellow bananas, which are growing rapidly in the Chinese market. .
"With the opening up of the Chinese market for mangoes, Cambodia will be able to grow as strong as bananas, with more job opportunities for farmers, raising their incomes and living standards," Wang said. He provides more benefits to the Cambodian people.
The Ambassador stated that the Chinese market is still open for other Cambodian agricultural products, such as Kampot durian, Kampot pepper, Kratie grapefruit and Kampong Speu palm sugar, all of which are potential commodities.
Oknha Hun Lak, CEO of Rich Farm Asia EK, an investment in mango plantations, said he was pleased for the private sector to open the way for Cambodia's fresh mangoes to China as a potential market for agribusiness. .
He said that for Cambodia, there is a lot of mango cultivation, in the past, the mango yield can not be exported directly to the Chinese market, but to sell mangoes to neighboring countries, they are washed and packaged for resale. Make Cambodia lose economic profits because we can not sell to the market and end users.
"Due to the efforts of the Ministry of Commerce, especially the Minister of Agriculture, HE Veng Sakhon, Cambodian agricultural products can be exported commercially to the Chinese market today," he said.
The tycoon said that in the first year, Rich Farm, one of the exporters, expects to export 10,000 tons of fresh mangoes to the Chinese market.
* Expanding vaccine vaccination strategy?
The decision to support Joe Biden's vaccine waiver comes as his people are under increasing pressure from a majority of Democrats in both houses of Congress who want the United States to share the vaccine with the world. The decision is a positive step back to the United States as a world power and moral leader.
As of this week, the United States has one of the highest immunization rates in the world, and Biden himself has fulfilled his promise to vaccinate 100 million doses in the first 100 days of his tenure. According to experts, as domestic vaccination progresses, it is time for Biden to come to the rescue of the world by sharing vaccines with other countries to challenge Chinese and Russian diplomatic vaccines.
In July 2020, Biden pledged, as a US presidential candidate, that he would not give up patents or intellectual property blocking global vaccinations, and he himself acknowledged the idea that "no one "It is safe unless everyone is vaccinated."
* Why are there disagreements over patent waivers?
Some European countries, such as Germany, have come out in opposition to the vaccine waiver, saying it will do nothing to help combat COVID-19 and even undermine the innovation and development of a new antiviral vaccine. Only.
According to the German government, barriers to vaccine production are not due to intellectual property, but rather to increasing production capacity and ensuring a fair distribution of vaccines, which are important issues to address. Berlin has also expressed support for the WHO-led COVAX mechanism, which aims to ensure that everyone around the world has equal access to vaccinations.
* Why do vaccine companies oppose patent waivers?
Joe Biden's decision to support is good news for a world that is in dire need of a vaccine. But there are also questions about when the vaccine patent waiver is approved, which rich countries will join Biden's plan? And more importantly, how many people will die before the negotiations take place?
US officials have acknowledged that more time is needed, as any decision must be made on the basis of "consensus" from all 164 WTO members.
