Ministry of Health Unveils Master Plan for 19 Kovid Vaccination Campaigns Nationwide (See 26 pages) (Video inside) (Phnom Penh): On May 7, 2021, the Ministry of Health released a master plan for 19 Kovid vaccination campaigns across the country, a roadmap for successful vaccination of people as planned.
The master vaccination plan aims to protect Cambodians from Kovid 19 by minimizing morbidity and mortality, protecting the health system and reducing the impact on socio-economic conditions.
In the preface to the 26-page master plan, Ms. Ou Vandin, Secretary of State for the Ministry of Health and Chair of the Vaccination Commission, highlighted that the "Master Plan for the Kovid-19 Vaccination Campaign Nationwide" Designed to complement the principles, procedures, strategies and activities to promote Kovid-19 vaccination in a timely, safe, effective, transparent and accountable manner.
She said the master plan was based on the "National Plan for the Kovid-19 Vaccination Campaign", which was launched by the Ministry of Health on January 18, 2021.
Ms. O Vandin highlighted that the ambitious goal set in the master plan for the nationwide Kovid-19 vaccination campaign is to vaccinate 10 million people by mid-2022.
She also expressed the hope that the active implementation of the master plan for the Kovid-19 vaccination campaign, coupled with the implementation of the "3 Do 3 and 3 preventive measures" and the strengthening of the national health security system, will provide an opportunity for Cambodia to receive Succeeded in the fight against Kovid-19.
The master plan aims to vaccinate 10 million people nationwide, or 62 percent of the population, and the coverage of 19 Kovid vaccines, more than 95 percent of the target population to be vaccinated by half. 2022.
