On April 26, 2021, the Chinese government, through the Chinese Customs Administration, officially recognized the list of 37 mango plantations and 5 registered packaging factories for exporting Cambodian fresh mangoes to China.
Through the capacity of these five packaging factories, Minister Veng Sakhon claims that Cambodia can export only about 100,000 tons of fresh mangoes per year to the Chinese market. But the minister expects more large companies to set up mango packaging plants and gain recognition from the Chinese customs administration, which could increase the number of factories and increase export volumes. Well.
Most of the fruit that can be exported to China is the mango variety that Cambodians like to grow and have a high yield.
According to the Minister, in Cambodia, by 2020, the cultivation of mango has increased to more than 130,000 hectares, which can yield from 1.6 million tons to 1.7 million tons.
He added that although Cambodia has not yet received approval to export fresh mangoes to China, in 2020, Cambodia exported 970,000 tons of fresh mangoes to neighboring countries for the year. By 2021, exports to neighboring countries are expected to reach more than 1 million tons.
Please be informed that for the export of mangoes directly to the Chinese market, the Ministry of Agriculture has been trying to negotiate to open the market for more than 3 years, only on April 26, 2021, the Chinese Customs Administration officially approved.
Cambodian fresh mangoes are the second fresh fruit after fresh bananas, which can be exported directly to China. This is another fruitful achievement born of the excellent cooperation between Cambodia and China. HE Dr. Seang Bunleang and Lok Chumteav Hun Bunthoeun Donate US $ 2,000 on the Occasion of the 158th Anniversary of the World Red Cross and Red Crescent Day, May 8, 2021
