Tbong Khmum Provincial Administration confirms that the fallen Po tree is not the Po Cheung Kal tree, the history of Tum-Teav love
(Tbong Khmum): The administration of Tbong Khmum province has officially confirmed that a large Po tree that was blown up by the wind and fell on the evening of May 6, 2021 yesterday is not the Po tree that is involved. With the history of the ripe love story.
The provincial administration came out after some rumors and misunderstandings on social media that the Po tree is located in Cheung Kal village, Mong Rieu commune, Tbong Khmum district, Tbong Khmum province, and that this fall is related to the history of Tum Teav's love.
The provincial administration emphasized that after receiving this information, the provincial administration officials immediately inspected the site and noticed that the fallen Po tree was not the Po Cheung Karl tree, the history of Tum and Teav.
However, the provincial administration has cooperated with professional officials to replant the Po tree in accordance with the correct technical specifications to preserve the green environment and preserve the religious beliefs of the Khmer ancestors.
