The Royal Government uses the "Blossom" strategy as a vaccination campaign to build socio-economic immunity in Cambodia, starting from the heart of the country
(Phnom Penh): The Cambodian government has decided to launch a "Strategic Plan for the Kovid-19 Vaccination Campaign to Create Socio-Economic Immunity in Cambodia by 2021".
The strategic plan prepared by the Supreme National Economic Council, published by the Office of the Council of Ministers, obtained by Fresh News on May 6, 2021, states that the Royal Government will use the "Blossom" strategy as a vaccination campaign. Socio-economic familiarity in Cambodia, starting from Phnom Penh, the heart of the country.
According to the Council of Ministers, Cambodia is expected to receive an additional 7 million doses of the vaccine from May to July and another 2.5 million doses from August to September, according to the Council of Ministers. The expected number of vaccines is sufficient to achieve the "Kovid-19 National Vaccine Campaign in High-Priority Areas to Build Socio-Economic Immunity in Cambodia by 2021."
On this basis, and based on the results of previous vaccination campaigns, immunization in high priority areas will be organized in three steps in accordance with the "Blossom" approach, starting in Phnom Penh, the heart of the country. And expand to the importance of the region and the socio-economic interconnection in all of the following high priority areas:
