(Phnom Penh): Measures to block Phnom Penh for 3 weeks have been completed by May 6, 2021. Mr. Keut Chhe, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, considered the measures to block Phnom Penh as a good, timely and effective measure to prevent Kovid 19.
Following the outbreak of Kovid 19 in Phnom Penh, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to close Phnom Penh for three weeks from April 15 to May 5. This is seen by health experts as a strategic measure to prevent the spread of Kovid 19.
At the same time, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration also cooperated with the Ministry of Health to take additional health measures, including the treatment of 19 Kovid patients, identification of stakeholders for sampling and transplantation, construction and preparation of new clinics and preparation. 19 more Kovid treatment facilities, etc.
Despite the Phnom Penh administration taking such action, the status of the Kovid 19 epidemic has not diminished. Because the implementation of these rules is not effective in preventing the transmission of Kovid 19, the Royal Government has reached out to put measures to block Phnom Penh.
Mr. Keut Chhe claimed that the blockade was aimed at protecting the lives of the people, cutting off transmission from one person to another, cutting off transmission from one area to another and preventing the spread to other provinces.
The deputy governor said that the measures to close the infection rate did not decrease, but the Phnom Penh administration can determine the location of the infection. He stated that at first, the spread of the disease in Phnom Penh could not be found anywhere, but after the closure, it was possible to know where the most severe infections were, where the moderate infections were and where the mild infections were.
"The Royal Government's measures are the most timely measures to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 in our country," he said.
After identifying 19 Kovid Outbreaks, the Royal Government has decided to lift the ban on Phnom Penh and Takhmao from May 6, 2021. Despite the removal of the blockade, the Phnom Penh Municipal Administration continues to introduce administrative measures for another week to control the situation of Kovid 19.
The Phnom Penh Municipal Administration continues to divide Phnom Penh into three geographical areas, but the yellow zone widens, while the red and yellow areas narrow down.
Although the yellow zone has a large visibility, Phnom Penh has not yet escaped the risk of spreading Kovid 19. In this regard, Mr. Keut Chhe continues to call on the people of Phnom Penh to pay attention to the strict implementation of health rules to prevent the spread of disease and to cut off transmission.
