Ministry requires candidates to be vaccinated against Kovid 19, if not able to be vaccinated, must have a certificate from the Department of Health
(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Public Works on May 6, 2021 confirmed that candidates who want to take the entrance exam within the framework of 6 ministries and institutions for 2021 must ensure that Kovid-19 vaccine has been vaccinated twice.
The six ministries are the Ministry of Public Works, the Ministry of National Assembly-Senate Relations and Inspection, the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries, the Ministry of Commerce, the Ministry of Water Resources and Meteorology and the Secretariat of Civil Aviation.
* 1: Candidates who have applied for the right to take the exam within the framework of the above 6 ministries and institutions must be guaranteed to be vaccinated against Kovid-19 twice.
* 2: On the day of the exam, all candidates must bring their ID card with them.
* 3: In case that the candidate is not able to receive the Kovid-19 vaccine, he / she must have an official certificate from the Capital / Provincial Health Department.
* 4: In case of any candidate who does not have Kovid-19 vaccination certificate or certificate from the Capital / Provincial Health Department, the Examination Organizing Committee will not allow that candidate to participate in the exam.
* 5: The Examination Organizing Committee will post the list of candidates to give the right to protest in case there is no exam name when the community event on February 20 is closed.
* 6: For the decision on allowing candidates to take the exam, the exam date and examination center, the examination organizing committee will inform later.
