On April 29, a group of experts in the field of immunosuppression, who will submit a proposal to the World Health Organization, released an evaluation report on the two Kovid 19 vaccines, which came to a comprehensive conclusion on safety and health. Efficacy of both Kovid 19 vaccines in adults.
According to the evaluation report released by the team, in the case of adults aged 18 to 59 who received two doses of SINOPHARM vaccine, the team has high confidence in the effectiveness of Kovid 19 vaccine. And there is moderate confidence in the low risk of severe adverse reactions after vaccination.
Currently, the global supply of 19 smallpox vaccines has plummeted. It was previously estimated that the World Health Organization (WHO) 's 199 Kovid vaccination plan would deliver 2 billion doses this year worldwide, but now only about 50 million doses are shipped. Moreover, as India has re-emerged with the 199 outbreak of Kovid, India has stopped exporting vaccines.
A global expert on immunodeficiency experts has called on the world to urgently need a Chinese vaccine.
