(Phnom Penh): Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, has come out to confirm that the vaccination operation for the people in the red area, which is an area facing the spread of Kovid 19 disease, is to vaccinate all the people. Samdech Techo Prime Minister emphasized that if the injection is not completed, it will not be withdrawn.
Confirmation of the commitment of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the leader who has always been highly responsible for the fate of the people in the work of vaccinating the people in the red area was made through a special voice message to the working group. Vaccination in the red area on Wednesday morning, May 5, 2021.
According to Samdech Techo Hun Sen, on May 11 and 15, Cambodia will receive another 1 million doses of vaccine from China. Therefore, Samdech Techo advised to prepare this vaccine in addition to the people in the red area.
In this message, along with the issuance of orders for the operation to vaccinate people until the end, Samdech Techo Prime Minister also called on people not to rush to get vaccinated, waiting for the arrangement of the vaccination team. The vaccine will be available to everyone, just before and after.
In this message, Samdech Techo Prime Minister has considered the people in the red area as a very serious victim. So make sure everyone gets vaccinated.
"The red zone is a high-risk area, people are blocked there," he said. "They are already struggling, so we need to get him to benefit first so that they can continue to be in the red zone, which can be considered a blockade by the Phnom Penh authorities."
In this audio message, Samdech Techo Hun Sen instructed the vaccination team to continue to organize a team of doctors to vaccinate in another red area that has not been vaccinated yet. According to Samdech, when the vaccine arrives on May 11, it will be injected in the red area that has not been vaccinated yet.
Samdech Techo also instructed the vaccination team to pay close attention to the area, especially the elderly with disabilities should be vaccinated first, and not to forget the monks in the temple to be vaccinated.
Cambodia started vaccinating people in the red zone on May 1. The Red Zone was covered by Army medics. The vaccination took place in four districts, including Kampol, Dangkor, Por Senchey and Meanchey, equal to 33 communes. The vaccination team deployed up to 54 injection sites and used up to 3,000 people.
In this voicemail, Samdech Techo Hun Sen expressed his pleasure at the rapid vaccination operation in four days, which could inject up to 150,000 people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen also praised the leaders and troops from the various divisions and the medical team of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces who came to help the people in the red area without fear or fear of danger. Samdech Techo also thanked for helping to distribute Samdech's help to the people in that area.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen thanked the people who wrote the letter and sent it via Facebook to thank the army, the doctors in the Red Zone, as well as the Royal Government. Samdech Techo sent a word of thanks from the people is an encouragement and a good cooperation between the injector and the injector.
