In this regard, the Ministry of Economy and Finance would like to recommend to all ministries, central administrative institutions, public institutions, administrations and units, councils, authorities and committees of the Royal Government on the measures to implement the 2021 budget editorial and budget efficiency as follows:
1: Translation of national budget expenditures
This national recurrence expenditure remediation measure is applied to non-staff expenditures by deducting expenditures at a percentage rate determined on a 50% credit basis, approved by the Financial Law for the year. 2021 for some expenditures that are not necessary or not very necessary and do not affect the work activities of ministries and institutions according to the following principles:
A. Ministry of Central Administrative Institutions
Separately, for ministries, institutions and units that have already signed a contract, 50% of the amount of fuel and lubricant is frozen at the supplier.
Loans that apply after deducting savings in accordance with the above principles are not allowed to be regulated for other expenditures, unless there is a separate decision of the Ministry of Economy and Finance to implement the highest priority activities of the Royal Government. Government.
Based on the above loan suspension policy, the Ministry of Economy and Finance will prepare an appendix to all relevant ministries, institutions and public administrative institutions regarding the size of the loan that has been revised, the expenditure and the credit that is still available to continue the expenditure problem.
On this basis, the relevant Ministries, Institutions and Public Administration Institutions need to adjust the total loan size, including the list of its pre-grant annexes, to the size of all expenditures deducted above and to the relevant sub-programs and activities.
B. Public Administration
Public institutions of administration, which receive 100% subsidy from the national budget, have been suspended from the loan according to the same principle of expenditure savings as applies to ministries and institutions at the central level, but with the exception of the temple repair and maintenance expenses of the APSARA Authority, Preah Vihear Authority and Sambo Authority. Prey Kuk.
In particular, public administration institutions that receive part of the national budget subsidy to meet the annual revenue-expenditure balance are allowed to use the budget at their equilibrium level, but there will be no additional budget credit in case of direct revenue. Decreased.
C. Units as councils, authorities and committees of the Royal Government
For the councils, authorities and committees of the Royal Government, which have budgets under the relevant ministries, institutions, the Ministry of Economy and Finance will examine the cost effectiveness to save and freeze actual expenditures in accordance with the pattern of the above principles. Each unit requests the expenditure to the Ministry of Economy and Finance.
The Ministry of Economy and Finance will prepare a table appendix to the seven relevant ministries on the size of the loan that has been revised, the expenditure and the credit that is still available to continue the expenditure problem. On this basis, the above seven ministries that receive regular public investment loans need to prioritize the project according to the existing level of budget credit.
2. Promoting and strengthening cost efficiency
* Strengthen operational costs, both in terms of value for money, in terms of type, quantity and technical efficiency.
* Prevent unnecessary or unprofitable or unprofitable expenses for ministries and institutions to achieve their mission goals.
* Restrict spending on individual ministries and institutions that do not affect domestic consumption.
Suspend the purchase of non-emergency and imported equipment and labels, providing new repair policies, except for existing building renovations.
* Strengthen the efficiency of inventory management and distribution of goods and services, as well as resources to reach the goal or hand in order to strengthen work efficiency.
* Facilitate the implementation of expeditious spending, especially the prevention and control of Kovid-19 disease, the cost to absorb the impact, the cost of intervention to support economic activities to respond appropriately to the actual situation in a timely manner.
