(Phnom Penh): General Sao Sokha, Deputy Commander of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Commander of the National Gendarmerie, on the night of May 4, 2021, requested the expulsion of a soldier (Gendarmerie) from the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces. This does not comply with the orders of the superintendent of leave, does not ask for permission and is found to have entered the red zone without permission.
The decision to expel the soldier from the army as the commander of the armed forces was confirmed by the general as a serious danger that the soldier may bring disease into the fort and cause Pass on to other forces (if positive Kovid 19 is found), so this one thing he must take decisive action no exception, no matter how strong this force or role.
General Sao Sokha's immediate action came after a military officer named Horm Vuthy failed to stand guard at his target and failed to report to his superiors for legal action and instead entered the Red Zone. Infected with Kovid.
General Sao Sokha told Fresh News on the night of May 4, 2021 that this soldier was on a mission to blockade Phnom Penh, but he did not ask the head of the unit. Discipline and enter the danger zone (red zone), so to prevent Kovid from entering other forces, it is necessary to take action by the forces by expelling them.
According to the general, if the disease is transmitted to other units and forces, there will be no force to implement the Royal Government's orders during this phase of the fight against Kovid.
