During a visit to the region on May 4, 2021, General Ith Sarath, Chief of Operation of the Kovid-19 Vaccination Campaign of the Ministry of National Defense in the Red Zone, expressed his remarks that the vaccination process The four-day vaccination in the red zone has progressed well.
General Ith Sarath pointed out that in four days, more than 100,000 people had been vaccinated in the Red Zone, and the number had risen steadily. This increase in injection is due to the increase in injection position up to 54 targets and increased injection force. Some of the target players, up to 8 players and 10 players.
The general also praised the efforts of the vaccination team and local authorities to work well together to provide information to the people and facilitate the vaccination process quickly.
However, there are some issues that need to be addressed. According to General Ith Sarath, in some areas, the vaccination team provided vaccination cards to many people, but people came without a license.
"The point where we need to continue to cooperate is between the injectors and the local authorities," said Ith Sarath. Some places are very good, good cooperation, people come to visit, some places seem to be a bit inconvenient because we distributed 2,000 cards and only 500 people came back. But when it comes to injecting people, there are a lot of unlicensed people, so we are working together to improve the place, ”he said.
The vaccine is given to the general population aged 18 and over. According to General Ith Sarath, the total number of people who will be vaccinated in the four red districts is 525,490,000.
The Royal Government plans to vaccinate the four districts in the red zone within a month, both the first and second doses.
General Ith Sarath expressed the army's commitment to speed up the operation to achieve the planned plan.
