(Phnom Penh): Mr. Kaing Tong Ngy, Director of the Communications Department of the Microfinance Association, said that during the closure of the Cambodian Microfinance Association encouraged customers not to worry too much about the debt owed by banks and microfinance institutions because now It is time to take care of your health and avoid unnecessary outings, which can lead to the risk of infection.
He stated that when there is a problem between the customer and the microfinance or bank, when the closure is completed, the institution will contact the customer to find out the customer's challenge and will discuss to find a joint solution to make the customer Can still continue their daily routine as usual.
"Customers do not have to worry too much because the closure will affect all customers, so each institution has a high understanding of customers. At the same time, at the end of the closure, we ask our customers to provide enough information to each institution so that the company understands the situation clearly.
He added that during the period of closure, if there are enough potential customers, ask customers to pay digitally or through a money transfer system where they can, and he definitely does not encourage customers to leave. Outside the house.
He added that for customers who can not use the digital money transfer system, customers can notify the institution or can suspend the payment for a while, waiting for the closure to be completed and repay.
He also reminded that the request for customers who can afford to pay is still normal because the institution itself is a private sector affected by the increase in operations as well as declining revenue, but microfinance institutions Not only do they try to protect themselves, protect their employees or their clients, MFIs also have to mobilize the resources they have to help those who are severely and moderately affected.
