(Kampong Chhnang): A couple working in a garment factory in Phnom Penh came to their hometown in Kampong Chhnang province, and the husband was found positive Kovid 19 on the evening of May 2, 2021, while the wife was negative. After testing with a quick instrument.
On the afternoon of May 3, 2021, Colonel Tim Chanthy, Police Inspector of Rolear Bier District, told Fresh News that the couple worked as workers in a garment factory in Phnom Penh and arrived in their hometown. Located in Prey Khmer village, Rolea Bier commune, Rolea Bier district, Kampong Chhnang province on the night of April 30, 2021.
Meanwhile, the car of the provincial health department also arrived at the same time. After the couple got into a car to perform rituals at the Municipal Model School in Kampong Chhnang, their two daughters were taken home by their mother in Kien Tama village overnight.
The inspector added that the couple lives in Kien Tama village, Kampong Os commune, Chulkiri district, Kampong Chhnang province, while the wife lives in Prey Khmer village, Rolea Bier commune, Rolea Bier district. Currently, a total of 20 people involved with the two couples have been tested by doctors.
Dr. Prak Von, Director of Kampong Chhnang Provincial Health Department, confirmed that the couple, Sam Sophearith, 25, had two daughters and lived in Prey Khmer Village, Rolea Bier Commune, Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province. A worker in a garment factory called T.L factory, which is located at the top of Phnom Penh.
After receiving the information that the couple left Phnom Penh to their home at the above address, more than 5 hours later, the team of the Provincial Health Department cooperated with local authorities to bring the couple to work. Chattaly Sak at the Municipal Model School in Kampong Chhnang immediately.
