German authorities crack down on child pornography site with more than 400,000 users
BERLIN: German prosecutors on Monday announced that they had cracked down on one of the largest child pornographic websites used by more than 400,000 member accounts. This was released by the AP on Monday, May 3, 2021.
German prosecutors said in a statement that in collaboration with German investigators, three suspects believed to be the site's administrator and a user, all German, had been arrested. Mid-April ago.
According to German authorities, the site has been hacked since at least 2019, and child sex offenders have been using it to exchange and view child pornography, most of them boys. All over the world.
German police have been investigating the site for months, along with its administrators and users, in cooperation with European police and authorities from the Netherlands, Sweden, Australia, the United States and Canada.
