Ministry of Education completes 191 Kovid vaccination campaign for more than 110,000 education workers nationwide
(Phnom Penh): The leadership and education staff of the Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports would like to thank Samdech Techo Prime Minister for deciding on the Kovid-19 vaccination campaign for education staff across the country. This strategic decision was ranked 17th by UNESCO as one of the countries in the world that has given priority to vaccinating teachers.
As of May 3, 2021, as a result, nationwide, the first phase of the campaign achieved both doses of vaccination for education staff, contract staff working in national, sub-national education units, public and private educational institutions, as well as A total of 116,563 employees of development partners in the education sector, accounting for 74% of the total 158,000.
In Phnom Penh, 24,800 people were vaccinated in two doses, and 45,400 people and monks were vaccinated in the second dose.
Overall, the first phase of the Kovid-19 vaccination campaign has received high praise from the general public, especially teachers, government officials, other ministries and civilians who came to receive the vaccination service, appreciating the preparation. The mechanism and operation are good, the compliance with the operating principles of the Ministry of Health is correct, the team in each vaccination center is friendly, coordinated and works responsibly.
The Ministry of Education, Youth and Sports would like to thank all the members of the Cambodian Higher Education Association, private companies and philanthropists for their financial support in the form of sanitation, beverages and food to support the vaccination team of this first phase of the campaign. .
Vaccination against Kovid-19 is an important opportunity to protect oneself, to protect one's family, and to have the opportunity to return to the reopening of the institution for further study of students in the future.
