(Kampong Cham): A drug distribution ringleader was arrested by Kampong Cham provincial police and confiscated more than 2 kg of drugs in Cheung Prey district.
Kampong Cham Provincial Police Commissioner Major General Em Kosal told Fresh News on the evening of May 3, 2021 that the operation to arrest the drug dealer was coordinated by Mr. Vong Bun Visoth, Prosecutor of the Prosecutor's Office. Accompanied by Kampong Cham Provincial Court.
Phay Seiha, 35, a resident of Svay Chou village, Russey Keo commune, Prek Prosop district, Kratie province, was arrested on May 1, 2021. The suspect was also the subject of an arrest warrant issued by Kampong Cham Provincial Court Investigating Judge Thorn Darith.
During the operation, the forensic experts confiscated two large packages of suspected drugs (weighing 2,037.71 grams) and two mobile phones.
Until May 2, 2021, with the permission of the above leadership, the police continued to investigate the above case together with the specialized force of Stung Trang District Police Inspectorate and the police force of Khpob Ta Nuon Administration and arrested Two more suspects. The above two people are traffickers who come to buy drugs from Phay Seiha to resell.
After arresting Phay Seiha, a drug user who called Phay Seiha to buy drugs, the police also arrested 13 more people. The suspects are currently being processed by the competent authorities to be sent to court for further proceedings.
