Comment: China welcomes international space cooperation with open attitude
The successful launch of the Tianhe core room is of special importance. In 1992, China's manned space mission set out a three-step development strategy: sending people into space and returning safely, and gaining a breakthrough in some of the key techniques of building space stations to build stations. Real space will solve the problem of using space that is relatively large and has long-term maintenance.
The successful launch of the Tianhe core room is the key to the third step, and this achievement is not easy. In the past, China has been excluded from the US-led International Space Station Club. In addition, Western politicians, who underestimate China's development, see space as a major battlefield for future arms races and wars, and are vigilant and vigilant in China's use of space technology.
But in the face of obstruction, China's space affairs have never been stuck, instead achieving some notable achievements, such as lunar exploration, Mars exploration, BeiDou satellite network assembly, and Successfully launch LongMarch transport rocket through innovative innovations. This time, China has taken an important step in building a permanent space station and is also important to the world.
Given that the International Space Station, which has been in operation for decades, will be able to retire between 2024 and 2028, the Chinese space station will probably be the only space station for humanity. Narrow Circle "China adheres to the principles of peaceful use, equality and mutual benefit, and develops together forever.
In the future, the world will have a new international space cooperation forum that is open and full of vitality. It will be the "great family in space" of real humanity. Retail fuel price from today to May 15: regular gasoline price 3,750 riel and diesel price 3,300 riel per liter
