* Do not publish content that obstructs or offends the efforts of life-saving personnel at the forefront, especially doctors and other competent authorities. * Do not be a tool of malicious information * Do not be a means of dissemination False information * Do not pose as a provocative, obscene, misleading, and misleading commentator.
At the same time, the Union of Cambodian Journalists recognizes that freedom of information and freedom of expression are very important in the process of democracy and social development. Of course, some sounds are not heard. Some problems are hidden or concealed, which requires the participation of the public to know and solve in time.
But all our actions must also be spiritually linked with ethics, ethics and responsibility, "spreading the truth but not blasphemy." I wish all the media and friends who like to use social media new successes in their careers and jobs, with a strong commitment to the nationalist ideal of "freedom under the spirit of national independence."
