It should be noted that each family received 10 kg of rice, 30 duck eggs, 1 box of noodles, 12 cans of fish, 12 cans of fish sauce and soy sauce, 1 kg of dried fish, 5 kg of mixed vegetables. Preah Vihear Provincial Police Officer Suspends Work on Two Dead Cows in Chep District
Preah Vihear: Two local cows out of a herd of cows were shot dead by police officers of Preah Vihear Provincial Police Inspectorate on the afternoon of May 1, 2013. This 2021 is in Chhep Lech village, Chhep Muy commune, Chhep district, Preah Vihear province.
The victim was a cow owner named Pheng Phal, 33 years old, and his wife Rim Seak, 32 years old, living in the above commune village. Separately, the police officer who shot the bull, a resident named Ear Kea Veasna, alias Pek, ranks as a lieutenant, with the role of Chief of the Anti-Drug Division of the Chhep District Police Inspectorate.
According to the villagers, the cows of this season are usually released only in the evening when the owner of the cows seeks to catch the cows and tie them at home. Separately, for the two cows that the police officer shot, he was walking in a herd of cows in the field of the police officer who had just sown, which made the officer angry and fired a gun.
After the incident, there was also a compromise, with the owner of the cow paying 5 million riel and the police officer giving only 4.5 million riel, but the owner of the cow refused and finally the officer gave 5 million riel to the owner of the cow. But the cow owner did not accept.
In connection with this case, Major General Sous Sok Dara, Preah Vihear Provincial Police Commissioner, issued a decision to temporarily suspend the work of this police officer, having to appear every working hour at the staff office of Preah Vihear Provincial Police to wait for a new decision. BREAKING: Siem Reap province finds another new Kovid-19 positive person
