(Phnom Penh): People living in the Red Zone, which is at high risk of contracting Kovid 19, were overjoyed when they were given the opportunity to be vaccinated against Kovid 19. They see the vaccine as a strong defensive force for health against Kovid 19.
The vaccination campaign for people living in the red area was held this morning, May 1, 2021. Vaccinations were conducted at 44 locations in 33 communes of Kampol, Por Senchey, Dangkor and Meanchey districts.
In order to facilitate the vaccination and speeding up, the vaccination team from the Ministry of National Defense cooperated with the local authorities to disseminate the vaccination and provided information cards to the people for them to complete in advance. Also.
Vaccination centers are organized in stages, including numbering, inquiries, immunizations and immunization cards. Vaccination sites are designed in conjunction with health measures to prevent Kovid 19, such as temperature measurements, alcohol spraying, masks and sitting gaps.
Ms. Sokha Dineth, a resident of Kambol district, clearly understands the benefits of Kovid 19 vaccine, which will help protect her health from Kovid 19 infection. "I came here for my own safety because we know that Kovid 19 has a worldwide epidemic," she said. "As a citizen, I have to get vaccinated."
Chit Visal, who lives in Kambol district, also understands the value of the vaccine. Visal is not worried about the health problems after the vaccination, as some have advertised.
Ms. Dineth and Mr. Chit Visal expressed their pleasure at the opportunity to be vaccinated. Residents of the two districts called on other unvaccinated people to get vaccinated to protect themselves from Kovid 19.
Cambodia has received more than 4 million doses of the vaccine and more than 1.3 million doses. The presence of a large number of vaccines and vaccinations is an effort and a serious consideration of the Royal Government of Cambodia, headed by Samdech Techo Hun Sen.
People who have been vaccinated highly appreciate Samdech Techo's leadership and consideration for the well-being of the people. The people who received the vaccine respectfully thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen and prayed for Samdech Techo to continue to lead the Cambodian ship forward.
