(Phnom Penh): Entering the third week of the closure of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng, the Governor of Phnom Penh, saw the good signs of cutting off 19 communicable diseases in Phnom Penh after the number of positive people was reduced to Next.
Phnom Penh has been experiencing an acute epidemic of Kovid 19 since February 20, 2021. It has been more than two months, but the epidemic has not abated. To eradicate the 19 smallpox outbreak in Phnom Penh, on April 15, the Royal Government decided to shut down Phnom Penh for two weeks. Due to the unresolved situation, the Royal Government continued to block Phnom Penh for another week from April 29 to May 5.
After the closure more than two weeks ago, although Kovid 19 has not been cured. But Khuong Sreng saw a good sign of the end of Kovid 19 after the number of positive people in the disease decreased slightly.
The Feb. 20 community event found 13,237 cases of Kovid 19 and 96 patients had died from the disease. Phnom Penh, which is also the center of economy, trade, culture and tourism, has the highest number of infections. This community event in Phnom Penh has a total of nearly 8,000 people, including more than 400 foreigners.
However, the number of cases in Phnom Penh in the last three days has been steadily declining. On April 28, Phnom Penh had 518 cases, and on April 29, Phnom Penh had 408 cases. On April 30, Phnom Penh had 331 cases.
The governor of Phnom Penh considered the signs of the reduction of Kovid 19 in Phnom Penh as a result of the closure of Phnom Penh. He said that the government's measures to block are already one step ahead of the situation, because if the government did not take such measures, the rate of 19 cases of Kovid in 19 countries in Cambodia is not known to spread. To what extent.
"Why do we dare to conclude that the closure measures of the past two weeks have been successful, because if the Royal Government does not issue an immediate ban on the closure of Phnom Penh, we can imagine whether Cambodia will spread the 19 cases of Kovid. How? This is the main point of closure in Phnom Penh, the disease may spread everywhere, so this is a success point, we are willing to suffer in places not to spread. This is what Mr. Khuong Sreng emphasized.
However, Mr. Khuong Sreng said that the eradication of Kovid 19 in Phnom Penh could not have been successful without the participation of the people and workers. The Governor of Phnom Penh continues to call on the people of Phnom Penh to cooperate with the authorities to eradicate the transmission of Kovid 19 successfully.
