(Phnom Penh): Nearly 200,000 families in the blocked area in Phnom Penh have received food donations from the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, as well as philanthropists, and no one has died of starvation. . This is the confirmation of the Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. Khuong Sreng.
Along with the measures to block Phnom Penh, Takhmao, as well as areas to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also reminded the authorities to focus on the needy people in the closed areas. That is, to provide food for them, not to deprive them of food.
The authorities and the army have arranged for food to be delivered to the people in droves, but not all of them. Mr. Khuong Sreng acknowledged that the distribution of food donations was not enough for the population.
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng, there are about 400,000 families in Phnom Penh who have to provide food, but now nearly 200,000 families have been distributed. He said the food distribution was focused on areas of need, such as the red zone, where people could not leave their homes.
Mr. Khuong Sreng stated that in order to solve this problem, he sent 50 tons of rice per district to the blocked areas to be distributed to the people when they received any reports or protests on social media.
The Governor of Phnom Penh also claimed that in addition to Samdech Techo's donation, the Phnom Penh Capital Administration also cooperated with private companies to sell some food items to people who could afford to live in the closed area to help alleviate difficulties when They can not get out of the house.
He claimed that the distribution of gifts to the people during the Kovid stage was very challenging, especially not being able to gather large numbers of people. Therefore, the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces, the Army Bodyguard Command, helped to bring all these rice and food items to the people's houses.
According to Mr. Khuong Sreng, the distribution of food to the people is done every day, with at least one day also distributed to 10,000 families, distributing day and night, hot and rainy without Do not push, and all forces never shout that tired.
Taking this opportunity, Mr. Khuong Sreng, as the Governor of Phnom Penh, also called on all people living in Phnom Penh, workers to see the important role of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, the Prime Minister of Cambodia, who has always been Front line to solve problems that arise.
"It is the pride of the Phnom Penh administration that to this day no one has died of starvation, this is the importance of our authority." This is the confirmation of Mr. Khuong Sreng.
In addition, the Governor of Phnom Penh also continued to call on philanthropists, companies, national and international civil society organizations from all walks of life to continue to contribute as much as possible in the spirit of a single Cambodian family to jointly fight against Kovid-19 through the administration of Phnom Penh. To continue to distribute to the needy people living in closed areas.
The Governor also welcomed all philanthropists, including political parties and national and international civil society organizations who want to help people in need, without discrimination or obstruction of humanitarian activities. This confirmation is in response to some advertisements and comments that the Phnom Penh Capital Administration does not block the assistance of some international organizations.
