(Phnom Penh): On the first day of vaccinating people in the red area, many people rushed to vaccinate, some at the wrong time organized by the authorities, leading to accumulation at the injection site. The Vaccination Commission has called on people to get vaccinated as scheduled by the authorities and do not worry about not getting vaccinated because the vaccine is ready for everyone. Especially when going to play, do not forget to bring identification documents such as ID cards.
May 1, 2021 is the day the sub-committee on the work of the Ministry of National Defense starts vaccinating 19 people in the red area in 33 communes of Khan Meanchey, Po Sen Chey, Dangkor and Kambol, with more than 47 people to be vaccinated. Ten thousand.
The vaccination process was conducted at 44 locations in the four districts. General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Executive Director of Vaccination Campaign, and Mr. Khuong Sreng, Governor of Phnom Penh, personally inspected the vaccination sites in the high-risk areas for 19 Kovid. .
Most of the vaccination sites were observed to be well-organized and in compliance with the health regulations of the vaccination team. But there are still some places where people have gathered and seem to have forgotten about the implementation of the 19 measures to prevent Kovid.
Mr. Ith Sarath said that some of the problems were caused by people rushing to get vaccinated without following the arrangements and instructions of local authorities.
Some people who go to get vaccinated do not seem to have been informed about the need for vaccination documents yet. Some people do not bring their ID cards, which are important identification documents for the vaccination. Some illiterate people also face difficulties when required to complete identification forms.
Responding to the problem of some people getting vaccinated without accompanying the documents, Mr. Khuong Sreng pointed out that his local authorities have village chiefs and commune officials all provide information at people's homes. From this information. Those who came without documents because they did not have time to play and the authorities have not yet given them any information.
The Capital Governor confirmed that “the people he invited were all informed by the village chief, the group chief, the commune chief, and what he had to bring. You came because you did not invite him, did not know what he had to take? This is why he does not have relevant documents.
In order to avoid congestion and lead to delays in the vaccination process, General Ith Sarath called on people to cooperate with the authorities and get vaccinated as planned without worrying about not getting vaccinated.
General Ith Sarath said that in the red zone, there were about 471,573 people and workers who were vaccinated during the campaign. The population to be vaccinated is equivalent to 943,146 doses of both vaccines.
Vaccination sites were set up in 44 locations in the 33 communes of Dangkor, Meanchey, Por Senchey and Kampol districts.
However, General Ith Sarath sees a number of gaps that need to be addressed in order to facilitate the vaccination, such as adding more doctors, increasing the number of vaccination sites and raising awareness of vaccination.
Mr. Khuong Sreng also thanked Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, as well as all the doctors who worked hard to vaccinate the people in the red zone. Areas at high risk for Kovid 19 infection.
