Cambodia for 22 years in ASEAN
(Phnom Penh): Cambodia, once an isolated country in Asia, went through decades of war and a genocidal regime between 1975-1979 that left millions dead and almost destroyed national infrastructure. Completely.
Under the win-win policy of Samdech Techo Prime Minister Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, at the end of 1998, Cambodia ended the war completely and there was real national unity and complete peace, which was a prerequisite for development in all areas up to Today, Cambodia is actively integrating itself into regional and global design.
During the past 22 years as an ASEAN member, what benefits has Cambodia gained and contributed to the building of this regional organization?
It was not until 1984 and the following year that five more countries in the region, including Brunei, Vietnam, Laos, Myanmar and Cambodia, became the youngest members of the association. ASEAN has three main pillars: a political-security community, an economic community and a socio-cultural community, all of which are interrelated.
Although not exactly what everyone expected, the benefits Cambodia gained after joining ASEAN were not insignificant. More or less, ASEAN is an important barrier to defending the sovereignty of member states, a core of regional design and an important diplomatic, political and economic gateway for its member states. The following are the main benefits that Cambodia enjoys as a member of ASEAN:
First, non-interference with other countries is ASEAN, no younger brother, no older brother, and does not interfere in the internal affairs of other member countries. At the same time, do not make relevant statements in the internal affairs of each member country. All member countries have the same rights and equal rights.
Second, the spirit of community is to work by the principle of consensus, no small country, no big country, no rich country, no poor country, which is clearly stated in the ASEAN Charter. If a consensus is not yet reached, it must be saved and the common good that ASEAN wants.
Third, integration is an opportunity for socio-economic development, which is an important attraction. In 2000, ASEAN launched a policy to reduce the gap between the old ASEAN countries and the new ASEAN countries, mostly in the Mekong region: Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam. The spirit of ASEAN is not to leave any member country behind, but to drive progress together.
Fourth, a wider diplomatic gateway for Cambodia within the ASEAN framework because ASEAN has many partners both in the region and outside the region, and Cambodia's membership is an opportunity to expand friendly relations and cooperation with all ASEAN partner countries. To bring many benefits for Cambodia.
Over the past 22 years, Cambodia has made significant contributions to the building of the ASEAN Community, the process of regional integration, and has contributed to the promotion and implementation of many ASEAN initiatives.
Cambodia has already chaired ASEAN twice, in 2002 and 2012. In 2022, Cambodia will take over the rotating chairmanship of ASEAN again.
However, the progress of ASEAN still faces some challenges between member states, especially non-members, regional and global powers. The economic gap between the old ASEAN member states and the new ASEAN members remains a problem. Cambodia, Laos, Myanmar and Vietnam still have low economic status compared to the other six new members of ASEAN.
However, Cambodia, as the host country, rejected the proposal, emphasizing that the South China Sea dispute should be resolved on a bilateral level between the Claimant States and should not be negotiated in a joint multilateral forum. In this regard, Cambodia has adhered to the core role and centrality of ASEAN, but has been accused by parties of demanding close and strong economic ties with China.
The current challenge is to address the spread of Kovid-19, and ASEAN, as one of the most active regional institutions, must strive to provide innovative solutions and promote regional coordination to respond to unpredictable challenges. Ever.
With the threat of the Kovid-19 epidemic, rivalries between the great powers will continue to be tense, and dividing the world into political, economic, commercial and technological aspects is a major concern. For 2022, Cambodia will assume the role of chair of ASEAN for the third time.
This role can be a source of pride and can also be a source of pressure. The Kovid-19 pandemic will remain a challenge for countries around the world that are struggling to find a way to recover from a near-collapse economy. Cambodia's need in 2022 as ASEAN chair is to continue to maintain and manage the environment conducive to peace and stability in order to sustain regional prosperity.
For the next 2022 ASEAN Chairmanship, we are confident that Cambodia will continue to push for a compromise settlement of the South China Sea dispute based on the DOC and push for the emergence of the COC. Appearance quickly.
The crisis in Burma will also remain a hot stone for Cambodia as ASEAN chair next year, as it is not hoped that it will be resolved anytime soon. Cambodia urges the ASEAN leaders' recommendations at the April 24, 2021 meeting in Jakarta to be implemented quickly and effectively.
Cambodia's rotating ASEAN chairmanship is not an individual success or failure for Cambodia. Cambodia's chairmanship is a rotation with previous presidents, so any achievements or progress are the joint work of the 10 ASEAN members. At the same time, many issues cannot be fully resolved under the rotating chairmanship of the ASEAN chair alone, sometimes for decades, such as the South China Sea, for example.
In 2022, Cambodia will launch new initiatives and continue to promote the implementation of ASEAN resolutions to make this regional organization stronger and more important.
