This morning, the army started vaccinating nearly 500,000 people in the red area in Phnom Penh.
(Phnom Penh): On the morning of May 1, 2021, the medical team of the army started a large-scale campaign to vaccinate Kovid 19 to the people in the Red Zone in Phnom Penh, which has nearly 500,000 people.
This morning, the vaccination process was inspected by General Ith Sarath, Deputy Commander-in-Chief, Joint Chiefs of Staff of the Royal Cambodian Armed Forces and Chief of Operations Campaign and Governor of Phnom Penh, Mr. KHOURN Sreng. .
Vaccination campaign for people in the red zone, which is a highly contagious area of Kovid 19, is a high consideration of the Prime Minister of Cambodia, Samdech Techo Hun Sen, so that people in the area at risk of contracting this disease. Vaccinated to protect their health from viral attacks.
The Red Zone in Phnom Penh, which will conduct a vaccination campaign for the people, is located in four districts: Dangkor, Meanchey, Por Senchey and Kampol, equivalent to about 33 communes.
General Ith Sarath said that in this red area, there are a total of 805,033 people and workers who need to be vaccinated. But about 29 percent of the population, 233,460 of whom have already been vaccinated, and about 100,000 workers, have already received the first dose and are continuing to receive the second dose.
As a result, 471,573 people and workers aged 18 and over in the Red Zone will be vaccinated during the campaign.
According to Samdech Pich Sena Tea Banh, Deputy Prime Minister and Minister of National Defense, the vaccination campaign in the red zone is scheduled to last only one month.
To achieve this plan, the Sub-Committee on Kovid-19 Vaccination of the Ministry of National Defense has assigned about 1,490 participants, including: 90 vaccination teams, 450 staff, 90 teams, 900 people, 10 transport teams, 50 people, 270 vaccination teams.
It should be noted that Cambodia has identified vaccination as a strategy to build immunity against the spread of Kovid 19. Phnom Penh and Kandal Province have been set out by Samdech Techo Hun Sen to give to the general public.
Cambodia started vaccinating people on February 10, 2021. To date, more than 1.3 million Cambodians, including foreigners, diplomats, and civil society officials in Cambodia have been vaccinated.
To date, Cambodia has received a total of more than 4 million doses of the vaccine for vaccination. Of those, 1.7 million doses were given by the Chinese government, 2 million doses were given by the Chinese government, and 324,000 doses were given by the quadrennial vaccine.
By speeding up the vaccination process for the people, Cambodia has become the second largest country in ASEAN, vaccinating more people.
