In the message of Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Fresh News stated, "On behalf of the Royal Government of Cambodia and on my own behalf, I am very pleased to join with my nephews, workers, employers and people. "All nations on the occasion of the 135th anniversary of International Labor Day on May 1 under the theme of peace, health and employment."
Samdech Techo Hun Sen continued that this topic really has a deep meaning and universal value, especially for the Kingdom of Cambodia, which has been plagued by devastating wars for centuries because only the preservation of Peace is the only way to develop jobs and job stability in the context of Kovid-19 disease.
May 1, International Labor Day in Cambodia is celebrated every year from the day of liberation from the genocidal regime on January 7, 1979 to the present. Although this year our nation and the world as a whole are facing Kovid-19, the Royal Government of Cambodia continues to commemorate this historically important day.
