The French minister said the infection was found among passengers from India and those with no contact with them.
However, he stressed that "the first three cases were not surprising. "There is an urgent need for medical intervention and that is what we are doing."
France has taken action for the third time since the end of March after suffering a rise in deaths and infections due to the spread of a new mutated virus.
