MOSCOW, April 30 (Xinhua) - The US Embassy in Russia on Friday announced that it would reduce its consular services to a minimum, citing restrictions imposed by Moscow on its mission workforce. According to a release by Xinhua.
The US Embassy in Russia will reduce the provision of consular services, leaving only emergency services for US citizens and the issuance of immigration visas to a minimum, the embassy said in a statement. Urgent from May 12 onwards. Non-immigrant visa processing for non-diplomatic travel will be suspended.
Russia's foreign ministry unveiled a retaliatory measure on April 16 against recent US sanctions, including a total ban on US diplomatic missions from hiring Russian citizens. Or a third country to an administrative or technical channel.
