The Secretariat of the Civil Aviation Authority of India announced on Friday that the suspension of international flights for passengers in and out of India in relation to COVID-19 will be valid until 23:59. The night of May 31, 2021. However, there may be exceptions for international flights for pure cargo and any international flights authorized by the relevant authorities.
International passenger flights have been suspended since India completely shut down the country in late March 2020 to prevent the spread of COVID-19. Domestic passenger flights resumed operations in India on May 25 last year after a two-month hiatus.
Since May 2020, India has operated a series of special international flights, and from July the same year, India also operated bilateral international flights with agreed countries. But after the resurgence of COVID-19 in April 2021, some countries decided to suspend flights between India.
