Siem Reap Provincial Administration Temporarily Closes Basket Market
(Siem Reap): The Siem Reap Provincial Administration on April 30 decided to temporarily close the entrance and exit of the basket market in Sangkat Svay Dangkum, Siem Reap City. The closure comes as one in 15 patients found positive on the night of the 29th have a history of entering and leaving the market.
A patient named Rith Kanthy, a 19-year-old male, lived in Vihear Chen village, Svay Dangkum commune between April 25 and 27. Therefore, to prevent eventual infection, the provincial administration decided to temporarily close the market pending further investigation.
This is the fourth market that the Siem Reap provincial administration has decided to temporarily close to prevent 19 cases of Kovid in the community. Previously closed markets include Zone 4 Market, which is now operating normally, but two other markets are still closed, including Lower Market and Wat Athvar Market. Minister of Commerce inspects the Royal Government's food reserve to supply the people
