Samdech Techo, Head of the Royal Government, stated that since becoming an ASEAN member, Cambodia has worked closely with other members to build a people-centered and people-centered ASEAN community in the spirit of ownership and acceptance. Joint responsibility.
He said that after a hard and soft political pursuit, Cambodia was decided by ASEAN to become the 10th member of its summit in Hanoi, Vietnam on April 30, 1999.
"ASEAN has become a core of Cambodia's foreign policy, which can be reflected by linking Cambodia's political, social and economic development to regional integration and international cooperation," he added. "Becoming a member of ASEAN is one of Cambodia's diplomatic successes in expanding its power and increasing its role in the region."
Please note that the Association of Southeast Asian Nations (ASEAN) is a regional organization with ten member countries in Southeast Asia, including Thailand, Malaysia, Singapore, the Philippines, Indonesia, Brunei, Vietnam, Myanmar, Laos and Cambodia. Cambodia joined on April 30, 1999 during a meeting in Vietnam.
