Because Siem Reap has set up health checkpoints for people on the border with Kampong Thom, they have been asked for information. Seeing that all the passengers were traveling from provinces that were at risk of contracting Kovid 19, authorities took them for medical tests and required them to be vaccinated.
Mr. Kros Sarath confirmed that many trips have been tested and required to perform cataracts, and by 8 pm on April 29, 15 positive people were found.
According to the director of the Department of Health, the 15 positive 19 cases of Kovid are mostly relatives and family members. That includes an 11-month-old baby.
