National Bank of Cambodia Signs MoU on Information and Knowledge Sharing Cooperation with Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications
(Phnom Penh): On April 29, 2021, the National Bank of Cambodia organized the signing ceremony of the Memorandum of Understanding (MoU) on "Cooperation in Sharing Information and Knowledge in Technology and Innovation" with the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications.
The MoU signing ceremony was attended by Ms. Chea Serey, Assistant Governor and Technical Director General of the National Bank of Cambodia, and Mr. Sok Puthivuth, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Posts and Telecommunications, as well as leaders and relevant officials of both institutions.
The MoU is aimed at strengthening cooperation between the National Bank of Cambodia and the Ministry of Posts in the field of technology and innovation, which will contribute to promoting innovation in the banking and financial sector. Efficiency and environment to contribute to the implementation of the Royal Government's digital economy development policy.
In addition, the MoU is also a nursery for strengthening the capacity and knowledge of technology and innovation of relevant officials of the two institutions to carry out various tasks more effectively in response to the needs and advances of current technology.
