(Phnom Penh): The Private Security Management Department of the General Commission of the National Police on April 29, 2021, summoned a security guard to interrogate and make an education contract after committing inappropriate acts by expelling and using violence against vendors. Vegetation in the Boeung Kak area where he is guarding.
The incident of violence occurred on April 28, 2021, by the name of Doung Pum, male, 33 years old, security guard of PPCC Company, current address: Toul Chan Village, Popel Commune, Ponhea Krek District, Kampong Cham Province. Selling vegetables at the company premises in Village 3, Sangkat Srah Chak, Khan Daun Penh.
After receiving this information, Lt. Gen. Lim Sokharaksmey, Director of the Private Security Management Department, immediately assigned a professional officer of the department in cooperation with the Phnom Penh Municipal Police to conduct a search.
As a result, officials from the Office of Investigation and Procedure of the Department of Private Security Management summoned 33-year-old Doung Pum for questioning. In front of the police, the private security guard clarified that there was indeed a case of violence with the people who sell mobile vegetables.
He added that prior to the violence, he had banned mobile vegetable vendors from entering the Boeung Kak Lake area, which was off-limits and affected the warehouse he was guarding, but he still did not listen. Stubborn continued to sell only to the point of violence, but did not cause serious injuries.
After the incident, vegetable sellers left the scene without complaining to each other. After the interrogation, the professional officers of the department and the authority of the Phnom Penh Municipal Commission educated, instructed and made a contract to stop committing violence against the people.
