(Preah Sihanouk): On April 29, 2021, Mr. Kouch Chamroeun, Governor of Preah Sihanouk Province and Chairman of the Provincial Administrative Unity Command, ordered the police to prepare a procedure for the expulsion of a Chinese national and not to allow him to enter the territory. Cambodia forever after this Chinese man disobeyed the ban and did not perform the duty of wearing a mask.
Kheang Phearum, spokesman for Sihanoukville Provincial Hall, told Fresh News this afternoon that police in Sihanoukville had arrested a Chinese man after he refused to follow the authorities' measures and instructions. Related to the ban on blockade in Sihanoukville to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 disease.
He said that after his arrest, the provincial governor ordered the competent authorities to prepare the eviction procedure and ban the Chinese man's name from entering Cambodia forever.
It should be noted that on April 22, 2021, the Preah Sihanouk Provincial Administration decided to block Sihanoukville for 14 days to prevent the spread of Kovid 19 after the disease has been recurring in recent days. .
The closure runs from April 23 to May 6. During the blockade, the provincial administration prohibits travel and departure, except in rare cases.
Businesses are also banned, except for businesses that are essential to people's daily lives, such as health services and food supplies.
The implementation of this measure shall take place 48 hours after the issuance of the Ministry of Health's press release issued on April 27, 2021.
The Ministry of Tourism also requested tourism operators, tourism associations, private sector development partners, relevant institutions and national and international tourists to implement this announcement effectively and responsibly.
