The Myanmar military has confirmed that unidentified groups launched rocket attacks on two air bases on Thursday, but no one was injured, with only minor damage. This was released by Reuters on Thursday, April 29, 2021.
In the first attack, four rockets were fired at an air base on the outskirts of Magway in central Myanmar in the early hours of the morning. Three rockets hit a field and another hit a road. However, a building at the military base was slightly damaged but no one was injured.
No group has claimed responsibility for the attack. Since the military took control of Myanmar in early February, fighting with ethnic armed groups has also increased significantly, with Myanmar launching several airstrikes along the border. The north and east of the country.
