UN-ESCAP was established by the United Nations in 1947, headquartered in Shanghai, China, with the aim of reviving the post-World War II regional economy and global economic crisis, and later relocated to Bangkok. Thailand in 1949.
UN-ESCAP plays a leading role in the region in observing, analyzing and addressing challenges in many areas, especially macroeconomic policy, poverty reduction and financing for development, trade and investment, transportation, environment and Development, Information and Communication Technology, Science, Technology and Innovation, Disaster Risk Reduction, Social Development, Statistics, Energy.
