Mr. Kros Sarath, Director of Siem Reap Provincial Health Department, told Fresh News on the morning of April 29, 2021 that the 19 positive Kovid patients, 47 years old, had kidney damage and lived in Leap Tong Village, Kampong Chen Tbong Commune, Stong District, Kampong Thom Province. . He came to receive dialysis services at the Siem Reap Provincial Referral Hospital.
With suspicion, the doctors took a quick test sample and found a positive result. The director of the Department of Health said that the patient had been admitted to the provincial hospital since the night of April 26. Only on the 27th did the dialysis be performed, but then, on suspicion, it was not until the 28th of April that the medical team performed a quick test.
Mr. Kras Sarath confirmed that after seeing such a positive result, health officials immediately tested more than 200 people in the hospital, and the results were all negative.
Officials are also investigating and closing down a number of other locations where the family of the 19-year-old Kovid has arrived in Siem Reap to prevent further outbreaks.
