(Phnom Penh): April 29, 2021 is the day to start the measures to block Phnom Penh and Takhmao City of Kandal Province for another 7 days to cut off the transmission of Kovid 19 disease in the community event on February 20. Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, emphasized that only strict implementation of the closure rule can cut off the transmission of Kovid 19 disease.
To facilitate the control of the situation of the spread of Kovid 19 in the measures to block Phnom Penh and Takhmao from April 29 to May 5, the Royal Government has divided the blockade into three types: red, yellow and orange. And yellow. The three areas have different measures to restrict traffic and business.
Speaking at a press conference on the closure of Phnom Penh and Takhmao on April 28, 2021, Mr. Nuon Pharath said that the closure is an important necessary measure to prevent the spread from the entire red zone as well as From the red to the yellow and other yellow areas, which can lead to greater risk.
In addition to the implementation of strict measures, the participation of the people is another necessary task for eradicating the transmission of Kovid 19. For this reason, Mr. Nuon Pharath called on the people to take all possible measures to cut off the spread of the disease and return to normal before February 20.
Mr. Nuon Pharath also asked for understanding on the emotional impact of the people's livelihood during the closure. He explained that people in closed areas may face difficulties, but still have better options than officials implementing measures because they can stay around families and prevent the spread of disease. But officials have no choice but to continue invading these dangerous areas to implement measures to cut off disease transmission and protect lives.
"All the people, parents, aunts and uncles, you have a choice at home, you can escape from the disease of Kovid 19, it is safe for the whole family, but we, the local officials, the forces, all the doctors, as well as the leaders have no choice, must "Efforts are being made to invade the Red Risk Zone for the sole purpose of preventing the spread of Kovid 19 and protecting the lives of parents and siblings." This is what Mr. Pharath said.
At the same time as the start of the 7-day blockade, Mr. Nuon Pharath also called on the people, traders as well as business owners in the yellow area to continue to implement the duty of the mask to keep the gap and the measures of the Ministry. Health. He warned that market traders and business owners are not consistent, and the authorities will take action to suspend sales and business activities.
On the night of April 29, authorities in communes and districts in Phnom Penh began to tighten the blockade, closing roads in the red and yellow areas.
