The anti-military movement has the backing of a number of ethnic rebel groups that control territory along the border with Myanmar. The Karen National Union (KNU), one of the most prominent ethnic groups, has also been among the junta's strongest opposition groups, condemning the use of violence against protesters.
Clashes with military forces in KNU territory along the eastern border with Thailand have escalated since February 1, with the military launching airstrikes last month, the first in a series of incidents. Karen State for more than 20 years.
