Relatives of the military who shot a plantation guard in O'Yadao district claim that it was not out of resentment, starting with the victim of previous violence against the gunman
(Ratanakkiri): Relatives of the military officer who shot a plantation guard in O'Yadao district, Ratanakkiri province on April 24, 2021 came out to claim that this incident was not a case of resentment, starting from the victim Accident in which the plantation guards used violence and smashed the car package of the previous gunman.
Ms. Te Chen, the wife of the military officer, confirmed this morning, April 29, 2021, at the time of the incident, she was also in the car with her husband, and before the explosion, the victim was sleeping. Thip chased, beat and insulted her husband, and violently smashed the car package, injuring her husband's arm. At that time, her husband decided to fire a weapon to threaten the victim.
However, the victim was not afraid, he kept shouting and threatening to kill her husband, so she decided to go to the victim, causing serious injuries and died at the hospital. Reference glass.
Surveillance cameras at the scene also showed that the gunman's car had left the scene, but the victim continued to chase and smash the package. However, after the explosion, the gunman did not escape, he drove to confess at the police station in O'Yadao district.
In addition, relatives of the victims said at the funeral that the two of them have never had any conflict with each other before, and the victim is like a family member living together. The perpetrators in the past also provided land for tractors to plow and plant potatoes to sell for their own money. The cost of the funeral is also borne by the perpetrator.
Please be informed that the assailant, a military officer who shot and killed a rubber plantation guard, was sent by the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police to the Provincial Prosecutor's Office on the afternoon of April 26, 2021. According to the police, the assailant was the owner of the rubber plantation and the victim was the guard of the rubber plantation.
Authorities say the cause of the fatal shooting was a rubber plantation worker who was hit by a pipe wrench, shattering his windshield and injuring his left arm. After the shooting, the assailant drove the car to confess at the O'Yadaw Police Inspectorate.
