General Knowledge: Margie Avery, the father of modern political philosophy, created a revolutionary mindset to stop believing in divine leadership.
(Italy): In ancient Europe, kings had the power to accomplish matters because they believed that the king was a deity and that the king's command was comparable to that of a deity. But then an Italian scholar revolutionized the idea of believing in divine leadership to believe in human leadership. Since then, politics and state leadership have undergone modern changes.
* Who is the scholar who created the revolutionary mindset to stop believing in such divine leadership?
* Career and work of Maggie Avery
Margie Averly served as a diplomat and political philosopher, writer, historian and war theorist, dubbed the "Father of Modern Political Philosophy."
He also worked as a diplomat for many countries, such as a spokesman for the Pope, the French Imperial Palace, the German Imperial Palace, as well as a spokesman for the Italian government. He worked like this until 1952, during which time he met with many top politicians, such as popes, emperors, and princes.
During his unemployment, Maggie Awley quietly wrote a number of documents, including those related to taxation, as well as works depicting the art of war and the history of Florence. His most famous work is the book "Samdech".
Another important theory is that "God can not do everything, so we must learn to be self-reliant and share the success that belongs to us." At this point, he means that the success of each person is from their own efforts, that is, there is no deity to help them reach success easily.
Indeed, during the Marxist period, many political theorists withdrew from the horizons of external forces, which they had previously considered to be able to bring them peace and prosperity. They turned their attention to the priority issues of the state and its purposes as a whole, shifting away from religious philosophy and turning to basic ideas and reflections that were perceived as the main tools. In search of true wisdom.
The main problem in that period was to ask the cause of the birth of the civil society and the formation of the state. At that time, the state was seen as an independent organization that was necessary to protect justice and ensure the safety of people. That period was the time when people turned from heaven to focus on earthly life and the destiny of real human beings.
At the same time, Ms. O Vandin also called on all people to remember and practice together in the spirit of solidarity, help each other, let's all be healthy, avoid this deadly disease and please Thank you for implementing 3 measures to prevent + 3 do not + vaccinate Kovid 19 + at home if you do not want to go out to avoid disasters, public health and the economy together.
