Minister of Commerce: Selling food in the red zone is a sale at a special favorable price, not a business
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Pan Sosak, Minister of Commerce, stated that the sale of food and groceries by the Ministry of Commerce to the people in the red area in Phnom Penh is in accordance with the Royal Government's instructions to help prevent the spread of Kovid disease. 19. The sale is at a particularly favorable price and there is regular monitoring of quality and price index.
The Minister emphasized that while inspecting the stalls selling food and groceries to people trapped in the closed area in Phnom Penh on April 28, 2021.
The Minister of Commerce claimed that all the goods were the reserve goods of the Royal Government and were sold to the people at the original price and the quality and price were carefully inspected by the General Department of PPR. .
"The supply of essential food and supplies to the people in the Red Zone has been carefully monitored for quality and price in order to prevent fraud, trade, inflate prices and advise all traders," he said. "Put a price tag on the item and do not let the price change arbitrarily beyond the price of the item sold before the closure."
Mr. Pan Sosak claimed that the Ministry did not do business with the people through the sale of all these goods. The Minister also called on all citizens in case of any fraudulent price increase, the Ministry encourages citizens to report immediately to the relevant authorities and relevant units of the Ministry or officials stationed at the stalls. To take timely action.
