(Phnom Penh): During the community event on February 20, 2,000 workers from 206 factories contracted Kovid-19 while more than 17,000 were required to be vaccinated.
At a press conference on the implementation of measures to block Phnom Penh and Takhmao on April 28, 2021, Mr. Heng Sour, Secretary of State of the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training, said that out of 206 factories, 134 are in Phnom Penh. Kandal Province has 23 factories, Takeo Province has 26 factories, Preah Sihanouk Province has 16 factories, Svay Rieng Province has 4 factories, Kampong Chhnang Province has 1 factory and Kampong Cham Province has 1 factory.
"There are a total of 1,673 workers positive for Kovid-19, of which 1,598 are in Phnom Penh," the spokesman said. There are more than 17,000 workers who work as carpenters. However, this number may increase or fluctuate because now in Ang Snuol district, Kandal province is testing positive for Kovid-19 and more directly affected people.
During the outbreak of Kovid-19, especially during the closure of Phnom Penh and Takhmao, more than 690 garment, footwear and travel accessories factories were affected and other small and large companies in Phnom Penh and Takhmao City, a total of more than 7,000 locations. The impact also affected a total of more than 1,200,000 employees.
Along with the closure of Phnom Penh and Takhmao, the Ministry of Labor has required factory owners to pay 50 of their April wages to their workers, and there should be additional support for them.
Heng Sour added that in addition to the Royal Government's support for workers, the Ministry of Labor also discussed with the Garment Manufacturers Association of the Garment Association of Cambodia (GMAC) as well as the Federation of Employers to ask employers to consider providing additional benefits to workers. Its employees in the spirit of humanity, solidarity and social responsibility.
The Secretary of State for the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training confirmed that for the needs of workers during the closure is 50 percent of wages in April.
At the same time, Mr. Heng Sour said that the Ministry of Labor has joined with the Ministry of Health and other stakeholders to facilitate the vaccination of workers in factories - enterprises, the first dose was given to 110 workers. The second dose was given to more than 10,000 people (the second dose was given three days ago).
He added that after the Royal Government and the Phnom Penh Capital Administration have identified red, yellow, orange and fast colors in Phnom Penh, the Ministry of Labor and Vocational Training has considered facilitating the issuance of permits to workers. They can be used to move from home to work in any area where the authorities allow the reopening of factories.
He added that after the above three color zones, more than 60 factories, enterprises and companies in Phnom Penh can be reopened, in which about 180,000 workers can return to work.
Heng Sour spokesman added that the Ministry of Labor will cooperate with relevant ministries and institutions. In particular, the Ministry of National Defense and the Ministry of Health to facilitate the vaccination of workers living in the red area, as well as vulnerable areas as instructed by the head of the Royal Government.
