Commentary: Why a plate of noodles can attract the attention of Xi Jinping, the supreme leader of China?
(Beijing): When it comes to snack noodles, many Cambodian friends also know. It is a specialty of Liaozhou, Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, China. In Cambodia, there are also many Guangxi people who go to work. Missing home food and Cambodia also has a lot of snails, so they brought snail-flavored noodles to Cambodia.
On April 26, Xi Jinping, China's top leader who is inspecting work in the Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region, arrived at the snail-flavored noodle industry to learn about the development of this unique business. Why can a bowl of noodles attract the attention of Xi Jinping, the supreme leader of China?
By 2020, in the context of the spread of Kovid 19 disease worldwide, sales of snail-flavored noodles will increase rapidly. In February 2020, the Chinese social network Weibo posted a post entitled "Why Noodles Are Still Not Delivered?" Has become a hot spot with 360 million viewers on this topic.
In recent years, Liaozhou has adhered to the concept of industrialization to develop the snail flavor noodle industry. With the continuous improvement of the technology of making bactericidal noodles by physical methods, machine packaging and other techniques, the efficiency of the production of package flavored noodles has been greatly enhanced.
In 2014, the first package of snack flavored noodles was established. Following a series of innovations, some companies have developed snail-flavored noodles that are durable and easy to transport, making snail-flavored noodles a popular food throughout China.
China's convenient freight traffic has shaped China's online economy. Under the influence of Kovid 19, people in the home watching live online sales have further spurred such economic development. Scallops have given birth to an industrial park.
At present, 34 snail-flavored noodles enterprises and related enterprises have been set up in the industrial park, which employs nearly 3,000 people and produces about 1.5 million packages of snail-flavored noodles per day.
Nowadays, due to its "sour and spicy" taste, snail-flavored noodles are popular all over China and have been exported to more than 20 countries and regions, which has become a business card of Liaozhou and an export agent. Foreign of Chinese food culture as well.
China's "14th Five-Year Plan" also mentions the development of specific industries by implementing measures appropriate to local conditions. A few days ago, China's National Bureau of Statistics released data showing that China's gross domestic product in the first quarter of this year rose 18.3 percent year on year.
(Phnom Penh): Mr. Nuon Pharath, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, said that the February 20 community event was a big disaster for Phnom Penh. In that, if no measures are taken to block Phnom Penh, the transmission of Kovid 19 will intensify and will continue to spread to the provinces even more.
At a press conference on the closure of Phnom Penh and Takhmao on the morning of April 28, 2021, Mr. Nuon Pharath said that the "February 20 community" event is like a disaster for Phnom Penh. But the Royal Government and the Phnom Penh authorities have not lost control of this contagious disease.
He added, "If we do not take action to close this two weeks, how will the positive people in Phnom Penh, who are facing this disaster, bring this disaster to the provinces?" This means that not only Phnom Penh and Takhmao, which are in a dangerous situation, other provinces may also face dangerous situations.
Please note that in order to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, the Royal Government of Cambodia has decided to block Phnom Penh and Takhmao for two weeks. As Kovid 19 has not yet recovered, the government has extended the measure for another week from April 29 to May 5.
Phnom Penh Capital Administration has divided 9 red areas, 41 yellow areas and 65 yellow areas.
However, Mr. Nuon Pharath called on people not to underestimate the situation and continue to strictly abide by the rules of the Ministry of Health. For the yellow area, Mr. Nuon Pharath emphasized that business owners must continue to perform their duties of wearing masks and keeping gaps. Otherwise, the authorities will take legal action.
(Phnom Penh): Despite the closure of Phnom Penh for two weeks, the number of 19 positive Kovid cases in Phnom Penh is still high every day. This raises questions about the effectiveness of the 19 cut-offs in the transmission of Kovid disease when blocking measures are applied.
In a press conference on the implementation of the closure measures on April 28, 2021, Mr. NUON Pharoth, Deputy Governor of Phnom Penh, confirmed that the high data of 19 cases of Kovid due to increased sampling of people in the area. Very contagious. According to Mr. Nuon Pharath, more than 5,000 to 6,000 samples are taken each day.
"We have set important targets for sampling, especially in the red zone," Nuon Pharath said. "This is why we have been able to mobilize large numbers of Kovid-19 carriers to remove them from their area to prevent further spread to others living in the area."
Mr. Nuon Pharath said that the February 20 community event in Phnom Penh found a total of nearly 8,000 Kovid 19 patients, including 442 foreigners. 6,898 people are being treated and 78 are dead. Ministry of Justice Introduces Measures to Prohibit Travel in and Out and Prohibit Jobs, Businesses and Businesses in the Loeung Tum Area
The following are the policies that Biden set out and addressed during the first 100 days of his presidency:
The United States is currently the most vaccinated country in the world, although COVID-19 has killed more than 572,000 Americans, the highest death toll in any country. More than 3,000 people died in one day when Biden took office. But now the average daily death toll is below 700, and the number of cases has dropped significantly.
* Employment and Economy
As of March, nearly 1 million jobs had been filled, compared with 379,000 in February. This improvement is expected to continue as the economy returns to normal and people gradually begin to return to normal living.
* Foreign policy
* Immigration
Joe Biden amended a large number of immigration policies left by Donald Trump. But Biden is facing a massive influx of immigrants on the border with Mexico. Biden canceled most of the border wall construction and lifted Trump's travel ban on the United States on people from 13 major Muslim countries and Africa.
Biden also promised to increase the number of immigrants allowed to enter the United States. But so far he has kept Donald Trump's COVID-19 policy. The policy has barred asylum seekers from arriving at the border for medical reasons. Human rights groups fear legitimate asylum seekers may be deported.
* Guns and Policies
The escalation of these shootings, including the violence against Asian Americans, which is rooted in the United States, is not easy for Biden to deal with. Biden called for restrictions on the use of firearms and ammunition, including a ban on the use of weapons of war or high-caliber firearms. But those measures still need parliamentary approval.
Biden proposed a multi-million dollar budget for a voluntary gun repurchase program. But he did not promise to report on the US Department of Justice's gun failures or reforms.
* Climate change
Joe Biden immediately fulfilled his promise by bringing the United States back into the Paris climate agreement after being ousted by Trump for national economic reasons. Biden has set out a strategy to achieve "carbon neutrality" by 2050. Biden, meanwhile, unveiled a $ 2 trillion infrastructure plan, including a multibillion-dollar budget for electric vehicles and clean energy.
In addition, the Biden administration has suspended new agreements for oil and gas exploration on US soil and waters, which is seen as a step towards a permanent halt. .
President Joe Biden's administration is seen as racially and ethnically diverse. Biden's administration includes 46 percent women and 50 percent non-white Americans, and to date, 21 of his 23 cabinet ministers have been elected by the Senate. Exit polls suggest more than half of Americans support Biden's work to date
