Cambodia seeks resilience, resilience, post-Kovid 19 crisis at UNESCAP 77th Annual Meeting of Least Developed Countries
In that statement, Senior Minister Ly Thuch mentioned five points, including:
2. Cambodia sees that the fight against Kovid-19 requires careful joint decisions within the framework of multilateralism, respecting international law and the sovereignty of individual nations, regardless of their existence or Poor. The importance and urgency of the supply and distribution of Kovid-19 vaccine, a global public commodity, must be conducted in a humanitarian manner for all countries, especially vulnerable ones.
3. Cambodia believes that countries should avoid protectionist policies and support vulnerable countries, especially financial support for vaccine production, to ensure that they have access to adequate vaccines.
4. Cambodia urges policymakers to implement their commitment to avoiding the effects of climate change, seeing a decline in greenhouse gas emissions during the Kovid-19 epidemic.
5. Cambodia urges the international community to take immediate action to prevent the recurrence of this disaster by establishing a repository of essential materials and protection equipment, funding for research and support for public health systems, and setting out models. Effective for providing first aid to those most in need.
He also stressed that Cambodia is ready to join regional countries and development partners in efforts to rehabilitate the socio-economic situation in order to continue to achieve the vision of sustainable development.
Those include:
1. Act as a staff of the Royal Government in liaising with UN-ESCAP and cooperating with ministries, national institutions, national and international organizations and development partners.
2: Study, research and provide input on the economic and social sectors in Cambodia and Asia-Pacific.
3. Contribute to building human resources in the economic and social fields through workshops and trainings.
4. Mobilize means and resources to contribute to the implementation of the Royal Government's political and strategic programs in the economic and social fields.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Calls on 5 Points for All Pregnant Women to Prevent Kovid-19 Infection
(Phnom Penh): Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross and National Outstanding Member of the Joint Action Plan of the United Nations Secretary-General for the Health of Women and Children, appealed to five pregnant women Preventing Kovid-19 infection.
Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen stated, "I would like to call on all pregnant women. Now is the time for you to be very careful to prevent yourself from being infected with Kovid-19 because Your condition during pregnancy is very easy to get infected, so please practice consistently:
2. Get regular check-ups with your doctor to monitor your and your baby's growth. Give birth at a health center or referral hospital and monitor the health of both mother and baby after delivery. Breastfeed and feed as directed by the Ministry of Health.
3. Contact the hospital / doctor immediately and follow the instructions of the doctor / midwife if you have a fever, cough or difficulty breathing.
4: In case you live in an area blocked by an outbreak of Kovid-19, please contact your midwife for a previous prenatal check-up to discuss personal and fetal health status. Child or postpartum care instructions.
5: Regularly monitor and properly implement the guidelines of the Royal Government, the Ministry of Health and the Capital / Provincial Administration to participate in ending the spread of Kovid-19 virus in Cambodia. I hope that together we will overcome this difficult opportunity together.
At the same time, Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen also called on all relevant institutions, national and international organizations, the private sector, development partners to continue to support investment in capacity building to implement key interventions in midwifery work at the global level.
