Commentary: Interfering with the issue of "democracy" as an excuse for the United States to be the world's biggest troublemaker
BEIJING: The commander of the US military in Afghanistan recently revealed that the United States and NATO have begun withdrawing troops from several military bases in Afghanistan. According to the plan, they will withdraw all troops before September 11. This means that the 20-year-long war will end abruptly, leaving only what is left of Afghanistan.
Since the 2001 war in Afghanistan, a total of 241,000 people have been killed, including about 71,000 civilians, even in the Afghan capital Kabul. Bombs and terrorist activities as well.
People are facing death all the time, social development is in a state of stagnation. Today, Afghanistan remains one of the least developed countries in the world. According to ADB statistics, 54.5 percent of Afghans live below the poverty line, 40.1 percent of adult workers earn less than $ 2 a day.
Ironically, as the main target of US attacks, during the outbreak of the war, the Taliban armed forces continued to make significant progress in the face of US aggression. It is a serious threat to the US-backed Afghan government.
No matter how excused the United States is and declares that it has "achieved its goal" in Afghanistan, it is impossible to cover up the sins, atrocities and defeats of this war, nor to cover up US crimes. Which has been causing unrest in the world as well.
