The following is the name of the patient of Kovid 19: The team of APSARA Authority started to rehabilitate in the western part of Angkor Thom
(Siem Reap): A team from the Water Management Department of the APSARA Authority has been working to restore the site in Angkor Thom. This first step takes place in the western part of Kasin or next to the Takeo gate of Angkor Thom, as the grass and small plants that grow on top of each other become thick and in some places almost invisible on the side. Below, there are about 6 feet of water.
Nhem Raksmey, technical officer of the Water Management Department, said that the department used nearly 40 people to carry out the work, which began on April 24. He said that the work faces some challenges, such as the venomous animals that live in the huts, which is a risk for the workers who cross the hut. In addition, it is difficult and can not do the job quickly, the beak is very thick, so there is a technique to cut small pieces to be easy to lift.
However, Mr. Nhem Raksmey confirmed that the team is looking for other ways to accelerate the work, such as the use of assistive devices to drag, which currently uses only direct manpower.
Please note that this thick grass is caused by small plants in the water, such as moss in the water for a long time, lack of adequate cleaning, causing thick snow to form. It is expected that the environment in the western part of Angkor Thom will become more beautiful and attractive after the restoration work is completed as planned and it will be easier to store more water than before.
