Agriculture Minister: China officially allows Cambodia to export fresh mangoes directly to China
(Phnom Penh): The Government of the People's Republic of China has officially authorized Cambodia to export fresh mangoes directly to China. This was confirmed by Mr. Veng Sakhon, Minister of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries on April 26, 2021.
Mr. Veng Sakhon stated, "On behalf of the leadership of the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries of Cambodia, I would like to express my deep gratitude to the Government of the People's Republic of China, especially the General Administration of Customs of the People's Republic of China for its official permission to bring in fruit. Fresh mango from Cambodia.
He added that the Ministry of Agriculture, Forestry and Fisheries will cooperate with the Chinese Ambassador to Cambodia to check the feasibility and timing of the official mango export ceremony from Cambodia directly to China. In this week.
The General Department of Agriculture has received applications for registration of mango plantations and packaging locations for the export of fresh Cambodian mangoes to 55 companies / plantation owners / farming communities. The General Department of Agriculture has also been receiving applications for registration of mango plantations.
On March 10, 2021, GACC experts in Guangxi Province inspected mango plantations and mango heat treatment plants via video system. As a result, after more than three years of market opening negotiations, on April 26, 2021, GACC officially approved the registration of 37 mango plantations and 5 registered packaging factories for fruit export. Fresh Cambodian mangoes to China.
Cambodian fresh mangoes are the second fresh fruit after fresh bananas, which can be exported directly to China. This is another fruitful achievement born of the excellent cooperation between Cambodia and the People's Republic of China. Dhammapalo Prak Khun, a Pali scholar, has died at the age of 96.
(Battambang): Preah Ang Thambalo Prak Khun, a scholar who is fluent in Pali and a veteran Pali teacher, at 3:50 pm on April 26, 2021, passed away. 96-year-old Preah Vossa is in old age, unable to get up and go to bed.
Venerable Dhammabalo Prak Khun is a Buddhist scholar born in Takeo province. He was born on March 5, 1926 into a farming family. As a child, he used to work as a monk, learn Dharma, and be proficient, especially in the Pali language. After graduating from the Senior Pali School in 1956, Dhammabalo left the seminary and became a teacher at the Ministry of Education.
Dhammapalo Prak Khun left a lot of works, especially the editing of Dharma books, Pali books, rewriting of Vesna Cheatak books and audio recordings of Dhammapada. Apart from this, Preah Ang Thambalo also spent money to build various achievements in some pagodas, including the Buddhist branch of Sihanoukville University, Battambang province.
Due to his hard work and dedication, Dhammapalo Prak Khun received great respect and admiration from the leaders, monks, laity and especially the students who had received knowledge from his father until he received the title. Honorary "Honorary Doctor of Pali".
At the end of his life, Dhammabalo Prak Khun decided to come and save the merits again at Wat Kantha Kod in Battambang province.
Russia expels Italian military diplomat in retaliation
MOSCOW (Reuters) - Russia's foreign ministry said on Monday that it had decided to expel a member of the Italian embassy in Moscow in retaliation. This is according to the release by the Xinhua news agency on Monday, April 26, 2021.
The decision was made in response to the dismissal of two employees of the Russian Embassy in Rome on March 31 over an espionage scandal.
