(Ratanakkiri): The assailant, a military officer who shot and killed a rubber plantation guard, was sent by the Ratanakkiri Provincial Police to the Provincial Prosecutor's Office on the afternoon of April 26, 2021.
According to the police, the assailant was the owner of the rubber plantation and the victim was the guard of the rubber plantation.
Authorities say the cause of the fatal shooting was a rubber plantation worker who was hit by a pipe wrench, shattering his windshield and injuring his left arm. After the shooting, the assailant drove the car to confess at the O'Yadaw Police Inspectorate.
It should be noted that on April 24, 2021, there was a dispute between a military officer and a rubber plantation worker, which led to the explosion of five handguns, one shot in the thigh near the right knee, two bullets in the left calf and two bullets in the chest. One bullet left his left forearm, causing his death when he was taken to Bor Keo District Referral Hospital at a rubber plantation in Kong Youk village, Patte commune, O'Yadao district, Ratanakkiri province.
The perpetrator was named Ly Theng Cheang, 48 years old, a military officer at the General Command of the Army Command, and the victim was named Rim Chantha, 37 years old, a rubber plantation worker, who lived at the scene.
In connection with the murder case, Rabo Randy, spokesman for the Ratanakkiri Provincial Prosecutor's Office, told Fresh News this afternoon that Deputy Prosecutor Han Sambath was being questioned for legal action.
Ministry recommends two types of tourism services to strengthen the implementation of stronger measures to participate in the prevention of Kovid 19
(Phnom Penh): The two main types of tourism services, accommodation accommodation, tourism, restaurant and canteen tourism services have been recommended by the Ministry of Tourism to strengthen the implementation of the measures of the Royal Government and the Ministry of Health, as well as tourism safety rules. Ministry of Tourism to help prevent the spread of Kovid 19 and end the event on February 20.
Therefore, in order to help prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease that may eventually occur in businesses, services, accommodation, tourism, restaurants and tourist restaurants in tourist destinations across the country, the Ministry of Tourism has introduced two main points, including:
First: For the target of Phnom Penh and Takhmao city of Kandal province
1.1: The Department of Tourism of Phnom Penh and the Department of Tourism of Kandal Province shall cooperate with the Administration of Phnom Penh and the Administration of Kandal Province and local authorities to further review and strengthen the implementation of tourism safety rules and all measures in force in the business of accommodation services, tourism, restaurants and canteens. Tourists operating food packaging.
1.2: The above two Departments of Tourism shall cooperate with the Capital and Provincial Administration and local authorities to continue to guide all the above business establishments, monitor all their employees who are obliged to conduct charter work and require the managers of the above business establishments to Inform local authorities of any suspicious cases of guests involved in Kovid-19 (after scanning the QR Code to prevent Kovid-19).
At this point, the Ministry of Tourism stated that "all of the above business establishments must implement all measures in force, in case of failure, implementation or improper implementation, the Department of Tourism must request the cooperation of local authorities to stop the business operation and continue the application procedure. "Implementing legal measures, especially the law on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 and other deadly and dangerous diseases."
Second: For other destinations of Kandal province besides Takhmao city and other provinces
2.5: Along with measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease, all the above business establishments must improve the quality of environmental-sanitation services and maintain the prices of products and services appropriately.
2.6: All the above business establishments must implement this circular effectively. In case of failure to implement or not in accordance with the content of this circular, the Department of Tourism must not allow the business to operate and may face legal measures in force, especially the law on measures to prevent the spread of Kovid-19 disease. And other vicious and dangerous diseases.
