First reopening day! Angkor receives 701 tourists as authorities continue to strengthen measures to prevent 19 Kovid
It should be reminded that on April 25, 2021, yesterday, APSARA Authority and Angkor Institute issued a joint announcement on the reopening of visits to temples and resold tickets to Angkor after a temporary suspension. 19 days, that is, from April 7-25, 2021.
Mr. Long Kosal stated that "The number of tourists who visited the temples in the whole Angkor resort for April 26, 2021, a total of 701 people, including 680 national tourists and international guests in 16 districts, including 5 monks.
He added that while Kovid 19 is spreading around the world, as well as in Cambodia, the APSARA Authority has taken great care to prevent the spread of the disease by requiring guests Tourists adhere to the "3 protection and 3 do not" measures when visiting the Angkor resort on this first day and beyond.
As always, APSARA Authority has set out measures for all officials and agents working at the temple site to implement this "3 protection and 3 no" measures on a regular basis.
Citizens and tourists alike, before visiting the temple, are required to wear a mask, wash their hands with alcohol and scan the QR Code to register to prevent Kovid 19 virus, especially not to gather or stand close to each other.
