Samdech Techo Hun Sen's appeal was made at the 77th Annual Meeting of the United Nations Economic and Social Commission for Asia and the Pacific (UN-ESCAP) on Monday. This April 2021.
For more than a year now, the whole world has been plagued by the Kovid 19 pandemic. The 77th Annual Meeting of UN-ESCAP was held under the theme "Post-Crisis Rehabilitation through Regional Cooperation in the Asia-Pacific Region" Each recurred after the Kovid 19 crisis.
In front of UN Secretary-General Ban Ki-moon and Secretary-General of the United Nations ESCAP, Ahmed Salasiya Alis-Jabana, as well as the leaders of other member states, Samdech Techo Hun Sen said that the 2021 global economy is expected to recover. However, there is still high uncertainty due to the risk of recurrence of the new wave of Kovid 19, especially through faster-than-expected mutations of the virus, which continues to disrupt economic life.
In this conference, Samdech Techo Hun Sen also gave some ideas to contribute to solving the global economic crisis caused by Kovid 19 disease. Samdech Techo provided the following ideas:
1: Continue to promote and support the principle of globalization through the opening up of international trade and strengthen the multilateral system, as well as give preference to developing countries to ensure the benefits of globalization. Globalization is analyzed equitably and effectively.
2. Promote digitalization by prioritizing digital government building and infrastructure development, support and encourage the private sector to embrace digital technology more widely, which will serve as a catalyst for new economic growth and contribute to competitiveness Compete and promote economic diversification.
