(Phnom Penh): The Ministry of Health on the afternoon of April 25, 2021 announced that three more Kovid 19 patients died.
The ministry said in a statement that the dead were all 79-year-old Cambodian women, 57-year-old men and 65-year-old women.
The Ministry states that the first case: a 79-year-old Cambodian woman living in Sangkat Phnom Penh Thmey, Khan Sen Sok, Phnom Penh. The patient arrived at the hospital on April 24, 2021 at 12:40 pm. Upon arrival at the hospital, doctors found that he had already died before entering the hospital.
As a suspicion, the body was analyzed by a team of doctors and the result was confirmed to be positive Kovid-19. The woman died before being admitted to hospital with Kovid-19.
Case 2: A 57-year-old Cambodian man living in Rolea Bier District, Kampong Chhnang Province arrived at the hospital on April 18, 2021 at 4:50 AM. Upon arrival at the hospital, doctors found that he had already died before arriving at the hospital.
As a suspicion, the body was analyzed by a team of doctors and the result was confirmed to be positive Kovid-19. Doctors' conclusion: The man died before being admitted to the hospital due to Kovid-19.
Case 3: A 65-year-old Cambodian woman living in Samrong Tong District, Kampong Speu Province died on April 24, 2021 at 2:00 AM. After receiving the information, the RRT team of Kampong Speu Provincial Health Department went to collect the body sample, as a result, confirmed that the body was positive Kovid-19. Doctors' conclusion: The woman died at her home of a person infected with the Kovid-19 virus.
The Ministry of Health has expressed its deepest condolences and deepest condolences to the bereaved families.
