Kandal Provincial Governor: Whichever factory finds 5% or more positive workers, the provincial administration will temporarily close the factory to prevent large-scale infections
(Kandal): Mr. Kong Sophoan, Governor of Kandal Province, announced that if the health team tests workers at any factory with a positive disease of 19% or more, the provincial administration will decide to close the factory temporarily. Once to prevent large-scale infection.
Provincial Governor Kong Sophorn said this in a meeting with representatives of five factories in Ang Snoul district who are suspected of being involved with workers with positive Kovid 19 on the afternoon of April 25, 2021.
According to the provincial governor, as a result of the discussions between the district administration and the representatives of the five factories, it was agreed that all workers should be tested using the Rapid Test immediately on key high-risk areas. 20% of the total number of workers, including security, managers, drivers, co-drivers.
Mr. Kong Sophoan continued that in case of positive Kovid-19 in the factory, they should be treated directly in the factory, while the direct victim must be treated in the factory for tenants. For those who have an address in the province, district, or commune, they will be sent to the provincial / district / commune for further management.
