Monks at Svay Romiet pagoda grow vegetables on pagoda grounds to reduce costs during the Kovid season
(Siem Reap): Monks at Svay Romeet pagoda in the eastern part of the western baray or Teuk Thla baray have been planting a variety of vegetables in the pagoda compound in an effort to reduce costs during the Kovid 19 disease.
His Holiness Vorn Lam, a teacher on the left of Wat Baray Mohan Ti Ratana, also known as Wat Svay Romeat, said that seeing the cost of the pagoda as well as the need to reduce costs, the monks could not go out to Ben Bat, so he prepared to plant. Vegetables in the vacant land around the pagoda. He added that before, the daily cost for cooking in the pagoda was 200,000 riel, but now it has been reduced to only 120,000 riel.
Having studied agriculture before, the land in the pagoda was vacant, and Vorn Lam began clearing land to grow vegetables in order to reduce some of the costs during the 19 19 period. Vegetables grown in Wat Svay Romeat include Tasak Nong, beans, lettuce and cabbage, which are natural vegetables that do not use chemical fertilizers.
