It should be noted that Samdech Techo Hun Sen led a delegation to attend the special ASEAN Summit on April 23.
The ASEAN Special Summit kicked off on April 24, 2021. The meeting was initiated by the President of Indonesia, Joko Widodo, and Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah Mujahideen of Brunei Darussalam as ASEAN Chair.
The meeting was also attended by leaders of other ASEAN member states, while Myanmar was represented by Ming Aung Lan, Myanmar's military chief, while Thailand, the Philippines and Laos were represented.
At the meeting, the first direct meeting of ASEAN leaders since the outbreak of Kovid 19, ASEAN leaders focused on accelerating the process of building the ASEAN Community, as well as initiatives to respond to the Kovid epidemic. 19 and efforts to restore socio-economic status, ASEAN relations with non-regional partners and the evolution of the international and regional situation of common interest and concern.
In this meeting, Samdech Techo Nguyen Tan Dung praised the progress made in the efforts to prepare a roadmap for implementation and the establishment of operational conditions for the appointment of a high-level working group to prepare the post-2025 ASEAN vision. Strive to fully implement the ASEAN Community Vision 2025 despite the Kovid-19 issue.
The special summit also raised the political crisis in Myanmar. With regard to the situation in Myanmar, ASEAN leaders have reached a remarkable common ground on important steps in easing tensions in order to have a constructive and gradual dialogue towards a peaceful and just solution. Long-term unity and return to democratic and peaceful change.
The ASEAN leaders stressed the importance of restoring a stable environment in Myanmar as soon as possible for the well-being of the people.
Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia adheres to the principle of non-interference in internal affairs.
Samdech Techo said that as a single ASEAN family, Cambodia has been closely monitoring the situation in Myanmar, which is becoming more acute and complex. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia supports the statement of the ASEAN Chair on February 1 and after the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting on March 2, which called on all parties to exercise restraint, avoid violence and negotiate a peaceful solution. .
"If there is mediation, the parties facing each other can return to a peaceful solution, that is, neither side wants to see bloodshed and loss of life," he said.
At the same time, Samdech Techo Prime Minister reiterated his position that as a member of the ASEAN family, Cambodia is always ready to join other ASEAN countries to help Myanmar return to poverty. In any role and in any form possible, it is in accordance with ASEAN principles and is acceptable to all parties.
In addition to the ASEAN Special Summit, Hun Sen also held bilateral talks with Indonesian President Joko Widodo. During the meeting, the leaders of the two countries expressed satisfaction over the development of bilateral relations and fruitful cooperation in various fields for the two countries.
The two leaders thanked each other for the vaccination of Kovid 19 to diplomats and people living in Indonesia and Cambodia and agreed on the importance of close ties in the fight against the epidemic, believing that both countries Will overcome this health crisis and will grow just as fast. The two leaders also expressed their condolences and condolences for the deaths of people affected by the epidemic.
