Samdech Techo Hun Sen: Cambodia is always ready to work with ASEAN to help solve the Myanmar crisis (Video inside) (Jakarta, Indonesia): With ASEAN to help resolve the political crisis in Myanmar.
The Prime Minister made this statement at a special summit of ASEAN leaders on April 24, 2021 in Jakarta, Indonesia. The meeting was initiated by the President of Indonesia, Joko Widodo, and Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah Mujahideen of Brunei Darussalam as ASEAN Chair.
The meeting was attended by other ASEAN leaders as well as the ASEAN Secretary-General, while the Myanmar side was attended by Myanmar Army Chief Ong Milang. However, the Prime Minister of Thailand, the Prime Minister of Laos and the President of the Philippines did not attend the meeting, only the Foreign Minister.
In addition to discussing ASEAN issues, the meeting also discussed Myanmar issues. Myanmar has been embroiled in a political crisis since early February after the military arrested Aung San Suu Kyi, leader of the Coalition for Democracy, and other party leaders after the party won national elections.
Proponents of her case have been working to make the actual transcript of this statement available online. The crisis in Myanmar has not been resolved by any party, only by sanctions from the West.
The ASEAN discussion in today's special meeting is the first discussion for a solution for Myanmar. In the presence of ASEAN leaders, including Mr. Ong Ming Lang, Samdech Techo Hun Sen emphasized that Cambodia adheres to the principle of non-interference in internal affairs.
Samdech Techo continued that as a single ASEAN family, Cambodia has been closely monitoring the situation in Myanmar, which is becoming more acute and complicated. Samdech Techo stated that Cambodia supports the statement of the ASEAN Chair on February 1 and after the ASEAN Foreign Ministers' Meeting on March 2, which called on all parties to exercise restraint, avoid violence and negotiate a peaceful solution. .
At the same time, the Prime Minister reiterated his position that as a member of the ASEAN family, Cambodia is always ready to join other ASEAN countries to help Myanmar return to poverty. In any role and in any form possible, it is in accordance with ASEAN principles and is acceptable to all parties.
At the meeting, other ASEAN leaders also stressed the importance of restoring a stable environment in Myanmar as soon as possible for the well-being of the people.
