(Jakarta, Indonesia): A special meeting of leaders of ASEAN member countries started at around 2 pm on Saturday, April 24, 2021 in Jakarta, Indonesia.
The meeting was attended by the leaders of ASEAN member countries as well as the Secretary-General of ASEAN, including Aung Min Lan, Myanmar's military leader. However, Thai Prime Minister Prayuth Chan-o-cha and Philippine President Rodrigo Duterte were not invited to attend, only the Foreign Minister.
The Cambodian Ministry of Foreign Affairs has stated that the meeting is expected to focus on three major topics: accelerating the ASEAN Community-building process, including initiatives to respond to the Kovid-19 pandemic; Socio-economic recovery efforts, ASEAN relations with non-regional partners and the evolution of the international and regional situation are of common interest and concern.
According to news reports, a special meeting of ASEAN leaders will discuss a solution to the current political crisis in Myanmar.
It should be noted that the special meeting of ASEAN leaders held in the difficult situation caused by the Kovid 19 epidemic is focused on medical examination and implementation of measures to prevent the transmission of Kovid 19. .
