(Phnom Penh): Food donations from Samdech Techo Hun Sen, Prime Minister of Cambodia, and Samdech Kittipritthbandit Bun Rany Hun Sen, President of the Cambodian Red Cross, were presented to monks at 24 pagodas in Phnom Penh on April 24, 2021.
The gifts of Samdech Techo and Samdech Kittipritthbandit were presented to the monks by Mr. Charles Van, Mr. Sao Phirun, Mr. Chin Bunthoeun and Mrs. Sbong Sambo, High Representative of Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit. The 24 pagodas that have received donations now are in 6 Khans: Khan Chamkarmon 4 Wat, Khan 7 Makara 3 Wat, Khan Boeung Keng Kang 1 Wat, Khan Daun Penh 5, Khan Sen Sok 6 Wat and Khan Russey Keo 5 Wat.
Seeing the shortage of monks in the pagodas during the implementation of measures to block Phnom Penh to prevent the spread of Kovid 19, Samdech Techo Hun Sen and Samdech Kittipritthbandit arranged for food to be donated. There are 142 pagodas in Phnom Penh. As of April 24, the team has donated to 111 pagodas.
