Wildlife surveillance using automatic cameras was carried out by research experts during the first quarter of 2021 and with the participation of local people of community patrols living near the sanctuary area. The team deployed automatic cameras at 11 key reindeer sanctuaries in the 50,093-hectare sanctuary, which is geographically located along the Mekong River.
The current record of reindeer provides additional vital scientific information and knowledge to the first record of this species in the sanctuary in 2020 to contribute to future survival both in Cambodia and in the country. Areas for this endangered species.
Neth Pheaktra, Secretary of State and spokesman for the Ministry of Environment, said that this was good news for Cambodia, as the species is still present in protected areas. Many wildlife, including rare species from around the world, are found in wildlife sanctuaries in Cambodia. Because Cambodia is completely peaceful, we have enough time and resources available to consider natural resource protection and conservation plans.
In the last 10 years, some species, including rare species, have been protected and conserved, some species have increased and some species have remained stable and some species continue to be threatened. But overall, we are proud to be involved in the conservation of wildlife in protected areas. The main problem that poses a threat to wildlife is hunting traps with recycled guns.
On behalf of the Ministry of Environment, Mr. Neth Pheaktra urges people who like to eat wild animals to stop immediately and participate in the protection and conservation of wildlife by saying no to wildlife to stop hunting and killing animals with traps. .
The senior official of the Ministry of Environment called on all Cambodians to join together to stop eating wild animals, use wildlife products, trade in wildlife, which can pose a high risk to human health, and come and join. Protect and preserve Cambodia's natural resources for the future of us and all our children. Siem Reap Provincial Administration Decides to Reopen Khvean Village, Kork Ta Chan Village, Phsar Zone 4 of Kork Chak Sangkat
